hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3601","Ishaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, saying: al-Zuhri heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madina when I was ten years old, and he died when I was twenty years old, and my mothers would urge me to serve him. He entered our house and we milked for him from a domestic sheep, and we mixed its milk for him with water from the well of the house. Abu Bakr was on his right and Umar aside. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank, and Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, give Abu Bakr. So he handed it to the Bedouin and said: The rightmost, then the rightmost."
"3602","Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out when the sun had declined and prayed Zuhr. When he gave the salutation, he stood on the minbar and mentioned the Hour, and mentioned that before it are great matters. He said: Whoever wishes to ask about something, let him ask about it; for by Allah, you will not ask me about anything but I will tell you of it as long as I am in this station of mine. Anas said: A man stood up to him and said: Where is my father's entrance, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The Fire. Then Abdullah ibn Hudhafa stood: Who is my father, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Your father is Hudhafa. Then he repeatedly said: Ask me. So Umar knelt on his knees and said: We are pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Messenger. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell silent when Umar said that. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, Paradise and the Fire were just now shown to me in the عرض of this wall, and I never saw like today in good and evil. Al-Zuhri said: And Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utba informed me: The mother of Abdullah ibn Hudhafa said: I never saw a son more undutiful than you; were you sure that your mother had not done something in the Jahiliyya so you disgrace her before the women? Abdullah said: By Allah, if he had attached me to a black slave, I would have joined him."
"3603","Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When dinner is placed and the prayer is called, begin with dinner."
"3604","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Ahwas ibn Jawwab narrated to us, Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ismail ibn Umayya, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raising his voice with Umra and Hajj."
"3605","Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray Asr, then one going would go to al-Awali while the sun was still high."
"3606","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid al-Hanafi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray Asr while the sun was white and alive; then one going would go to al-Awali and reach it while the sun was still high."
"3607","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Amr ibn Asim narrated to us, Abu al-Awwam narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: On the day of Hunayn, the people fled from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib and Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered it to be called out: O Companions of Surat al-Baqara, O company of the Ansar. Then the call intensified among Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj. When they heard the call, they came forward; by Allah, I likened them only to camels coming to their young. When they met, the fighting grew fierce. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Now the oven has heated. He took a handful of white pebbles and threw them, saying: They are defeated, by the Lord of the Kaba. And Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, was that day the fiercest of the people in fighting before him."
"3608","Abu Musa Harun ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Umar ibn Hafs, from Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to be safe, let him keep to silence."
"3609","Harun ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, Yunus ibn Yazid al-Ayli narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman would walk in front of the funeral bier."
"3610","Kamil ibn Talha narrated to us, Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, Uqayl narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever loves that his term be extended for him and his provision be spread out for him - I think he said: in - his provision, let him join his ties of kinship."
"3611","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Usama ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: And al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Anas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from Uhud, he heard the women of the Ansar weeping. He said: But Hamza has no mourners. That reached the women of the Ansar, so they wept for Hamza. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slept, then woke while they were weeping. He said: Woe to them, they have continued weeping since today; let them weep, but let them not weep over one who perishes after today."
"3612","Hudhayl ibn Ibrahim al-Jummani narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Zuhri, of the descendants of Sad ibn Abi Waqqas, narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant says: there is no god but Allah, in an hour of night or day, but what is in his record of evil deeds is effaced until it is settled with the like thereof of good deeds."
"3613","Wahb ibn Baqiyya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do not envy one another, do not compete with one another, do not hate one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and be servants of Allah as brothers; and it is not lawful for a man to abandon his brother for more than three days."
"3614","Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drink milk, with Abu Bakr on his left and a Bedouin man on his right. So he gave the Bedouin his remainder, then said: The rightmost, then the rightmost."
"3615","Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us, Abu Damra narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: Ubayy would report that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The roof of my house was opened while I was in Makkah; Jibril descended and opened my chest, then washed it with Zamzam water. Then he brought a basin of gold filled with wisdom and faith, poured it into my chest, then closed it."
"3616","Abu Ali al-Hasani narrated to us, Ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Musa ibn Uqba, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, who said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not help in the ransom of al-Abbas? He said: Not even a dirham."
"3617","Abu Bakr ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from al-Layth, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Abu Dharr would report to him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The roof of my house was opened while I was in Makkah; Jibril, peace be upon him, descended, opened my chest, then washed it with Zamzam water. Then he brought a basin of gold filled with wisdom and faith, poured it into my chest, then closed it. Then he took my hand and ascended with me to the sky. When he came to the lowest sky, Jibril said to the keeper of the sky: Open. He said: Who is this? He said: Jibril. He said: Is anyone with you? He said: Yes. He said: And has he been sent for? He said: Yes. So he opened. When we rose above the lowest sky, behold a man sitting with black forms on his right and black forms on his left; when he looked toward his right he smiled, and when he looked toward his left he wept. He said: Welcome to the righteous Prophet and the righteous son. I said to Jibril: Who is this? He said: This is Adam, and these black forms on his right and his left are his children; the people of the right among them are the people of Paradise, and the black forms on his left are the people of the Fire; when he looks to the right he laughs, and when he looks toward his left he weeps. He said: Then Jibril ascended with me until he came to the second sky, and said to its keeper: Open. Its keeper said to him like what the keeper of the lowest sky had said, and he opened. Anas said: He mentioned that he found in the skies Adam, Idris, Musa, Isa, and Ibrahim, but he did not specify their stations, except that he mentioned that he found Adam in the lowest sky and Ibrahim in the third sky. Anas said: When Jibril and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Idris, he said: Welcome to the righteous Prophet and the righteous brother. He said: Then I said: Who is this? He said: This is Idris. Then I passed by Musa, and he said: Welcome to the righteous Prophet and the righteous brother. I said: Who is this? He said: This is Musa. Then I passed by Isa, and he said: Welcome to the righteous Prophet and the righteous brother. I said: Who is this? I think he said: Isa. Then I passed by Ibrahim, and he said: Welcome to the righteous Prophet and the righteous son. I said: Who is this? He said: This is Ibrahim."
"3618","Humayd ibn al-Rabi al-Khazzaz narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Maryam al-Misri narrated to us, Nafi ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Uqayl ibn Khalid, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ayyub, the Prophet of Allah, was in his affliction eighteen years; near and far abandoned him, except two men among his brothers, among his most devoted brothers, who would come to him morning and evening. One of them said to his companion: Do you know, by Allah, Ayyub has committed a sin no one has committed? His companion said: What is that? He said: For eighteen years Allah has not had mercy on him to relieve him. When they went to him in the evening, the man could not restrain himself until he mentioned that to him. Ayyub said: I do not know what you say, except that Allah knows that I would pass by two men disputing while mentioning Allah, and I would return to my house and make expiation on their behalf, out of dislike that Allah be mentioned except in truth. He said: He would go out to relieve himself, and when he finished, his wife would hold his hand until he arrived. One day he was late for her, and it was revealed to Ayyub in his place: Strike with your foot; this is a cool washing place and drink. She waited for him, then met him waiting; he came to her with Allah having removed his affliction, in the best state he had been. When she saw him, she said: May Allah bless you, have you seen this afflicted Prophet of Allah? By Allah, I never saw anyone resembling him when healthy more than you. He said: I am he. And he had two threshing floors: a threshing floor for wheat and a threshing floor for barley. Allah sent two clouds; when one of them was over the wheat threshing floor, it poured gold into it until it overflowed, and the other poured silver onto the barley threshing floor until it overflowed."
"3619","Humayd ibn al-Rabi al-Khazzaz narrated to us, Ruwaym al-Qari narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sad informed us, from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, Anas informed me: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the land is fertile, dismount from your backs and give it its due of pasture; and when the land is barren, pass over it with its marrow; and upon you is traveling by night, for the land is folded at night."
"3620","Humayd narrated to us, Shababa ibn Sawwar narrated to us, Uqayl narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he wanted to combine Zuhr and Asr while traveling, would delay Zuhr until the time of Asr entered, then combine them."
"3621","Qasim ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, from his father, from Yunus al-Ayli, from al-Zuhri, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, place in Madina double the blessing that is in Makkah."
"3622","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Diama narrated to us, Umar ibn Sharik narrated to us, from his father, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dye with henna, for it is pleasant in smell and calms dizziness. Abu Yala said: I do not know whether this Sharik is Ibn Abi Namir or not."
"3623","Abu Khaythama Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Ibn Abi Uways Ismail narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Sharik ibn Abi Namir, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: A man traveled with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and cursed his camel. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O servant of Allah, do not travel with us on a cursed camel."
"3624","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abi Namir, who said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would hear the crying of a child behind him and lighten the prayer, fearing that his mother would be put to trial."
"3625","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi Yazid al-Sadai narrated to us, Abbad al-Minqari narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Madina when I was eight years old. My mother took my hand and went with me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, there remains no man or woman among the Ansar but has gifted you a gift, and I cannot afford a gift to gift you except this son of mine; so take him, let him serve you as long as you wish. So I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ten years; he never struck me a blow, never insulted me, never scolded me, nor frowned at me. The first thing he enjoined upon me was saying: O my son, conceal my secret and you will be a believer. My mother and the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would ask me about the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but I would not inform them of it; and I will never inform anyone of the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And he said: O my son, upon you is perfecting ablution; your two guardians will love you and your lifespan will be increased. O Anas, be thorough in washing from major impurity, for you will come out of your washing place with no sin or fault upon you. He said: I said: How is thoroughness, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Wet the roots of the hair and cleanse the skin. O my son, if you can remain always in ablution, for whoever is met by death while in ablution is given martyrdom. O my son, if you can remain always praying, for the angels pray for you as long as you pray. O Anas, when you bow, place your palms firmly on your knees, spread your fingers, and raise your elbows from your sides. O my son, when you raise your head from bowing, settle every limb in its place, for Allah will not look on the Day of Resurrection at one who does not straighten his back between his bowing and prostration. O my son, when you prostrate, place your forehead and palms firmly on the ground; do not peck like the rooster, nor squat like the dog - or he said: the fox. Beware of turning in prayer, for turning in prayer is ruin; if it must be, then in the voluntary prayer, not the obligatory. O my son, when you leave your house, let your eye not fall upon anyone of the people of the qibla but you greet him with peace, for you will return forgiven. O my son, when you enter your home, greet yourself and your family. O my son, if you can wake and sleep with no deceit in your heart for anyone, for it is easier for you in the reckoning. O my son, if you follow my counsel, nothing will be more beloved to you than death."
"3626","Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abd al-Karim ibn Malik, from Ikrimah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said to a man driving a sacrificial camel: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Then ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Even so. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it without wounding it."
"3627","Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Sam'an ibn Malik al-Maliki narrated to us, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdullah, he said: A Bedouin came and urinated in the mosque, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that his spot be dug out and a bucket of water poured over it. The Bedouin said: O Messenger of Allah, a man loves a people though he has not done their deeds? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man is with whom he loves."
"3628","Abu Hisham narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same."
"3629","Sufyan ibn Waki' narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for nine years, and he never said to me for something he disliked: Why did you do it? And he never said for something that pleased him: How well you did it."
"3630","Sufyan narrated to us, Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the same."
"3631","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ya'la narrated to us, my father narrated to me from Ghaylan ibn Jami', from Uthman ibn al-Mughirah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, he said: Anas narrated to me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pronouncing the talbiyah for Hajj and Umrah together, and my knee was touching his knee."
"3632","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, he said: While I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were coming out of the mosque, a man met us at the entrance of the mosque and said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What have you prepared for it? The man seemed to hold back, then said: O Messenger of Allah, I have not prepared for it much prayer, nor fasting, nor charity, but I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: Then you are with whom you love."
"3633","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, from Shu'bah, he said: I heard Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Anas, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When is the Hour? He said: What have you prepared for it? He said: I have not prepared for it much prayer, nor fasting, nor charity, except that I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: Then you are with whom you love."
"3634","Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn al-Munkadir and Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, they heard Anas ibn Malik saying: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) Zuhr in Madinah as four, and Asr at Dhu al-Hulayfah as two."
"3635","Salih ibn Malik narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr in Madinah as four, and he prayed Asr at Dhu al-Hulayfah as two while traveling to Makkah."
"3636","Muhammad ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Mu'ammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Anas, he said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) Zuhr in Madinah as four, and he prayed Asr at Dhu al-Hulayfah as two."
"3637","Amr ibn Malik al-Basri narrated to us, al-Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq al-Qurashi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I asked my Lord for the heedless playful ones among the offspring of mankind, so He granted them to me."
"3638","Zuhayr and Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us, they said: Ibn al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Rabi'ah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent at the age of forty, and he passed away at the age of sixty, and there were not twenty white hairs in his beard or his head."
"3639","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Rabi'ah, he said: I heard Anas saying: There were not twenty white hairs in the head and beard of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3640","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Rabi'ah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal will emerge from the Jewish quarter of Asbahan, with him seventy thousand Jews wearing al-sijan."
"3641","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, he said: I heard Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: There were not twenty white hairs in the head and beard of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3642","Zuhayr narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, he said: I heard Rabi'ah al-Ra'y saying: Anas ibn Malik said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away at the age of sixty, and there were not twenty white hairs in his head and beard."
"3643","Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Ghadidi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Qurrah, that Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman narrated to him that he witnessed a gate of Baqi' al-Gharqad where a crowd was seated behind him, among them Anas ibn Malik, he said: So I heard him mention the description of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and among what he mentioned he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became a prophet at the age of forty, stayed in Makkah ten years and in Madinah ten years, and passed away at the age of sixty, and there were not twenty white hairs in his head and beard."
"3644","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, he said: And Rabi'ah informed me that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had wavy hair, neither straight nor very curly, he was radiant fair, neither dark nor stark white, he was of medium build among the people, neither short nor conspicuously tall, he was sent at the age of forty, stayed in Makkah ten years and in Madinah ten years, and passed away at the age of sixty, and there were not twenty white hairs in his head and beard."
"3645","al-Hasan ibn Ismail Abu Sa'id narrated to us, at Basra, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The leaders are from Quraysh; when they judge they are just, when they covenant they fulfill, and when mercy is sought from them they show mercy."
"3646","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Sukayn ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Sayyar ibn Salamah al-Riyahi Abu al-Minhal narrated to us, he said: I entered with my father upon Abu Barzah al-Aslami, and in my ears that day were two earrings - meaning: a boy - so Abu Barzah said: I praise Allah that I have come to dispraise this clan of Quraysh; so-and-so here fights for worldly gain, and so-and-so fights for worldly gain - meaning: Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan - until he mentioned Ibn al-Azraq, then he said: The most beloved people to me are this matted-haired company, whose bellies are lean from the wealth of the Muslims, whose backs are light from their blood. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The rulers are from Quraysh - three times - you have a right over them, and they have a right over you as long as they do three things: when they judge they are just, when mercy is sought from them they show mercy, and when they covenant they fulfill; and whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."
"3647","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Mus'ab, he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pronouncing the talbiyah for Hajj and Umrah together."
"3648","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Mus'ab, he heard it from Anas, saying: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating while squatting, eating eagerly, while he was dividing it and sending me with it; I think he means: dates."
"3649","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, from Humayd and Mus'ab, they heard Anas informing the people that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while at al-Bayda - and he was riding behind Abu Talhah - pronouncing the talbiyah for Umrah and Hajj."
"3650","Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted the Ansar land in Bahrayn as a grant, so they said: O Messenger of Allah, and our brothers among the Muhajirun, so grant them too. So he said: You will meet after me favoritism, so be patient until you meet me."
"3651","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, they said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Humayd and Yahya ibn Sa'id both informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the best quarters of the Ansar? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The quarters of Banu al-Najjar, then the quarters of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then the quarters of Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, then the quarters of Banu Sa'idah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And in every quarter of the Ansar there is good. And one of them said in his narration: And he raised his voice with it."
"3652","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will face after me favoritism, so be patient until you meet me."
"3653","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id - Abu Khaythamah said: meaning al-Ansari - he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: A Bedouin urinated in the mosque, and his companions wanted to stop him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave him. Then he ordered water, and it was poured over it."
"3654","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Dawud ibn Qays narrated to me, from Dawud ibn Qays, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Anas ibn Malik, that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying on a donkey - while going to Khaybar - with the qiblah behind him."
"3655","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, from Anas, he said: A Bedouin entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then stood toward a side of the mosque, and the people shouted at him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) restrained them until he finished, then he called for a bucket of water and poured it over the Bedouin's urine."
"3656","Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj and others narrated to us, they said: Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Isa ibn Maysarah, from Abu al-Zinad, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prayer is the light of the believer."
"3657","Harun ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Isa al-Hannat, from Abu al-Zinad, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Envy consumes good deeds as fire consumes wood, and charity extinguishes sin as water extinguishes fire, and prayer is the light of the believer, and fasting is a shield from the Fire."
"3658","Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala' al-Hamdani narrated to us, Umar ibn Ubayd al-Tanafisi narrated to us, from Umar ibn al-Muthanna, from Ata' al-Khurasani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he stepped aside to relieve himself, then he came and said: Is there any water? So I brought him a waterskin of water, and he performed ablution with it, then wiped over the two leather socks."
"3659","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Umar ibn Ubayd al-Tanafisi narrated to us, from Umar ibn al-Muthanna, from Ata' al-Khurasani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and he stepped aside to relieve himself, then caught up with me and said: Is there any water? So he performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks, then caught up with the army and led them in prayer."
"3660","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ata' ibn Abi Maymunah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the privy, I and a boy would bring him a waterskin and a short spear, and he would clean himself."
"3661","Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah al-Fazari narrated to us, from Ata', from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over his son Ibrahim, and pronounced four takbirs over him."
"3662","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to me, he said: I heard Ata' ibn Abi Maymunah narrating, I know it only to be from Anas, that no retaliation case was ever brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except that he commanded pardon in it. So Ibn Bakr said: I used to narrate it from Anas without doubt in it, so they said: From Anas? So I said: I know it only to be from Anas."
"3663","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' and Ghundar narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Ata' ibn Abi Maymunah, he said: I heard Anas saying: I used to go out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I was a boy, with me a waterskin and a short spear, and he would relieve himself, then perform ablution."
"3664","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, Rawh narrated to me, from Ata' ibn Abi Maymunah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out alone to relieve himself, so I would bring him water and he would wash with it."
"3665","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Ata' ibn Abi Maymunah, from Anas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out to relieve himself, he would go far until he was hardly visible."
"3666","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr in Madinah as four, and two at Dhu al-Hulayfah - meaning Asr."
"3667","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah al-Wasiti narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Abu Maslamah, from Abu Nadrah, from Anas, he said: Umm Sulaym sent me with fresh dates to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a tray at the first ripening of the palm fruit, he said: So I entered upon him and placed it before him, and he ate some of it, then he took my hand and we went out, and he had recently married Zaynab bint Jahsh. He said: So he passed by some of his wives, and with them were men talking, he said: They congratulated him and the people congratulated him, saying: Praise be to Allah who has delighted your eye, O Messenger of Allah. So he went on until he came to Aishah, and with her were men, he said: So he disliked that, and when he disliked something it was known from his face, he said: So I came to Umm Sulaym and informed her, so Abu Talhah said: If it is as this son of yours says, something will happen, he said: So when evening came, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and ascended the pulpit, and recited this verse: O you who believe, do not enter the houses of the Prophet except when permission is given to you for food. He said: So he commanded the veil."
"3668","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Abu Maslamah, he said: I said to Anas: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray in sandals? He said: Yes."
"3669","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Ya'qub ibn Zayd ibn Talhah, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: A man was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for his harm to the enemy and diligence, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not know this one. He said: Rather his description is such and such. He said: I do not know him. While we were thus, the man appeared, so he said: This is he, O Messenger of Allah. He said: I did not know this one; this is the first horn I have seen in my nation; in him is a touch of Satan. When the man drew near he greeted, and he returned the greeting, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I adjure you by Allah, did you say to yourself when you appeared before us that there is no one among the people better than you? He said: O Allah, yes. He said: So he entered the mosque and prayed, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Bakr: Stand and kill him. So Abu Bakr entered and found him praying, so Abu Bakr said to himself: Prayer has sanctity and right, and if only I had sought the Messenger of Allah's order, so he came to him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Did you kill him? He said: No, I saw him praying, and I saw prayer has sanctity and right, and if you wish that I kill him I will kill him. He said: You are not his man. Go you, O Umar, and kill him. So Umar entered the mosque and found him prostrating, so he waited long, then said to himself: Prostration has a right, and if only I had sought the Messenger of Allah's order, for one better than me had sought his order, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Did you kill him? He said: No, I saw him prostrating, and I saw prostration has a right, and if you wish that I kill him I will kill him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are not his man. Stand, O Ali, you are his man if you find him. So he entered and found him already gone from the mosque, so he returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Did you kill him? He said: No. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had he been killed today, no two men of my nation would have differed until the Dajjal emerges. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to them about the nations, saying: The nation of Musa split into seventy-one sects, seventy of them in the Fire and one in Paradise, and the nation of Isa split into seventy-two sects, seventy-one of them in the Fire and one in Paradise. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And my nation exceeds both groups together by one sect: seventy-two in the Fire and one in Paradise. They said: Who are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The united communities. Ya'qub ibn Zayd said: And Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, when he narrated this hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), would recite Quran in it: And among the people of Musa is a nation who guide by the truth and by it they do justice. Then he mentioned the nation of Isa, saying: And if the People of the Book had believed and feared, We would have expiated their sins, up to His saying: Evil is what they do. Then he mentioned our nation: And among those We created is a nation who guide by the truth and by it they do justice."
"3670","Muhammad ibn Bakkar, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Attaf ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, he said: I prayed Zuhr with Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, then we went to Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, and when we entered upon him he said: Have you prayed? We said: Yes. So he said: O girl, bring me water for ablution. I have not prayed behind an imam after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whose prayer resembled the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than this imam of yours. Zayd said: And Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz would complete the bowing and prostration, and lighten the standing and sitting."
"3671","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The excellence of Aishah over women is like the excellence of tharid over all other food."
"3672","Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdillah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The excellence of Aishah over women is like the excellence of tharid over all other food."
"3673","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The excellence of Aishah over women is like the excellence of tharid over all other food."
"3674","Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The excellence of Aishah over women is like the excellence of tharid over all other food."
"3675","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abdillah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: A sheep was milked for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and its milk was brought, he said: So he called for water and poured it over the milk, then drank, while Umar was facing him, Abu Bakr was on his left, and a Bedouin on his right, he said: So Umar said: Abu Bakr is next to you, he said: So he said: The right-most ones first, and he handed it to the Bedouin."
"3676","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Za'idah, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reclined at Bint Milhan, he said: So he dozed, then woke smiling, he said: So she said: O Messenger of Allah, what are you laughing at? He said: Some people of my nation riding in this green sea, their likeness is like kings on thrones. I said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to make me among them. He said: O Allah, make her among them. He said: So she married Ubadah ibn al-Samit, and she rode the sea with Bint Qarazah, and when she returned her mount threw her off and killed her, and she was buried."
"3677","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ma'mar al-Ansari narrated to us, and he mentioned similar to the hadith of Ibn Abi Shaybah, from Husayn, except that in the hadith of Zuhayr: Until when she returned, she rode a mount at the shore, and it threw her off, so she fell and died."
"3678","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ma'mar ibn Hazm, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laid his head in the house of Ibnat Milhan, who was one of his maternal aunts, then raised his head and laughed, so she said: What makes you laugh, O Messenger of Allah? He said: People of my nation riding this sea, like kings on thrones. So she said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to make me among them. So he supplicated for her to make her among them. Then he laid his head, then raised it and laughed, so she said: What makes you laugh? So he said the same as he said the first time. So she said: Supplicate to Allah to make me among them. So he said: You are among the first, and you are not among the last. He said: He said that two or three times. He said: So Ubadah ibn al-Samit married Bint Milhan, and he rode with her the midst of the sea, and when she was at the shore she rode her mount, and it threw her off, so she fell and died."
"3679","Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Khalid al-Zayyat narrated to me, Dawud ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ma'mar ibn Hazm al-Ansari, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him - raising the hadith - he said: The newborn, until he reaches the age of accountability, whatever good he does is written for his father or for his parents, and whatever evil he does is not written against him nor against his parents. When he reaches accountability, the pen runs upon him, and the two angels with him are commanded to guard and to be strict. When he reaches forty years in Islam, Allah secures him from the three afflictions: madness, leprosy, and vitiligo. When he reaches fifty, Allah lightens his reckoning. When he reaches sixty, Allah grants him turning to Him with what He loves. When he reaches seventy, the people of heaven love him. When he reaches eighty, Allah writes his good deeds and overlooks his evil deeds. When he reaches ninety, Allah forgives him his past and future sins, and grants him intercession for his household, and he is Allah's captive on His earth. When he reaches the most feeble age so that he knows nothing after knowledge, Allah writes for him the like of what he used to do in his health of good, and if he does an evil it is not written against him."
"3680","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Verily supplication is not rejected between the adhan and the iqamah, so supplicate."
"3681","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Isra'il ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam al-Saluli, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Supplication between the adhan and the iqamah is answered, so supplicate."
"3682","al-Azraq ibn Ali Abu al-Jahm narrated to us, Hassan narrated to us, Yusuf narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever mentions me, let him send blessings upon me, and whoever sends one blessing upon me, Allah sends ten upon him."
"3683","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl informed us, from Yunus ibn Amr, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever asks Allah for Paradise three times, Paradise says: O Allah, admit him to Paradise; and whoever seeks refuge with Allah from the Fire three times, the Fire says: O Allah, protect him from me."
"3684","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no servant who asks Paradise three times except that Paradise says: O Allah, admit him to Paradise; and there is no servant who seeks refuge with Allah from the Fire three times except that the Fire says: O Allah, save him from me."
"3685","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Burayd ibn Abi Maryam, from Anas, he said: In the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we used to steep fresh and dried dates, and when the prohibition of wine came down we poured them out of the vessels, then left them."
"3686","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas, he said: Jibril came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day while he was sitting grieved - and some of the people of Makkah had struck him - and said: What is wrong with you? He said: These people did such and such to me. He said: Would you like me to show you a sign? He said: Yes. He said: So he looked at a tree beyond the valley and said: Call that tree. He said: So he called it, and it came walking until it stood before him, so he said to it: Go back. He said: So it returned to its place."
"3687","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, while he was sitting grieved after some of the people of Makkah had struck him. He said: So he said: These people did such and such to me. He said: Would you like me to show you a sign? So he looked at a tree beyond the valley and said: Call that tree. So he called it, and it came walking until it stood before him, so he said to it: Go back. So it returned until it went back to its place. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It suffices me."
"3688","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to often say: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, we believe in you and in what you brought, so do you fear for us? He said: Yes, hearts are between two fingers of the fingers of Allah, He turns them."
"3689","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas, he said: Among the supplication of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he used to often say: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we believe in you and in what you brought, so do you fear for us? He said: Yes, hearts are between two fingers of the fingers of Allah, He turns them."
"3690","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out angry and addressed the people, saying: You will not ask me about anything today except that I will inform you of it, while we thought Jibril was with him. So a man stood to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, we were recently in pagan ignorance; who is my father? He said: Your father is Hudhafah, the father to whom he was attributed. So he asked him about things. So Umar ibn al-Khattab stood to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, we were recently in pagan ignorance, so do not expose our faults. He said: Will you disgrace us by our secrets? Pardon us, may Allah pardon you. We are pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Messenger. He said: So it was lifted from him, then he looked and said: I have never seen like today in good and evil; Paradise and Hell were shown to me below the wall, and I have never seen more veiled faces than that day."
"3691","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Ubaydah narrated to us, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us one day angry, and we thought Jibril, peace be upon him, was with him until he ascended the pulpit, and I never saw a day with more weeping veiled ones. He said: Ask me, for by Allah you will not ask me about anything except I will inform you of it. A man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, who is my father? He said: Your father is Hudhafah to whom you are attributed. Another stood to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, am I in Paradise or in the Fire? He said: In the Fire. A man stood to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, is Hajj upon us every year? He said: Had I said yes it would have become obligatory, and had it become obligatory you would not uphold it, and had you not upheld it you would be punished. Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: We are pleased with Allah as Lord, Islam as religion, and Muhammad as Prophet, and do not disgrace us with our secrets, and pardon us, may Allah pardon you. He said: Then he became cheerful, then turned toward the wall and said: I have never seen like today in good and evil; Paradise and Hell were shown to me behind this wall."
"3692","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Ubaydah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: They once struck the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he fell unconscious, so Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, stood calling: Woe to you! Would you kill a man for saying my Lord is Allah? They said: Who is this? He said: The son of Abu Quhafah, the madman."
"3693","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Sufyan, Amr ibn Amir narrated to me, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform ablution for every prayer. He said: And you? He said: Ablution suffices us as long as we have not broken it."
"3694","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Qasim al-Rahhal, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered a ruin belonging to Banu al-Najjar to relieve himself, then came out to us frightened, saying: Were it not that you would not bury one another, I would have asked Allah to let you hear of the punishment of the grave until you hear it."
"3695","Ahmad ibn Isa al-Misri narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Amya' narrated to me, that Sahl ibn Abi Umamah narrated to him that he and his father entered to Anas ibn Malik in Madinah at the time of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz when he was governor, and he prayed a light prayer as if it were a traveler's prayer or close to it. When he gave salam, he said: May Allah have mercy on you, tell me, was this prayer obligatory or something you volunteered? He said: It is obligatory, and it is the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I have not missed except something I forgot. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Do not be hard on yourselves lest Allah be hard on you, for a people were hard on themselves and it was made hard on them; those are their remnants in monasteries and cloisters: And monasticism they invented, We did not prescribe it for them. Then they came in the morning and said: We will ride and look and take lesson. He said: Yes. So they all rode, and there they were by ruined dwellings whose people had perished and vanished and been swept away, collapsed upon their roofs. They said: Do you know these dwellings? He said: How well I know them and their people; these are dwellings whose people transgression and envy destroyed. Envy extinguishes the light of good deeds, transgression confirms that or denies it, the eye commits adultery, and the palm, foot, hand, tongue, and private part confirm that or deny it."
"3696","Husayn ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had supplications he never left; he would say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from anxiety, sorrow, grief, inability, laziness, miserliness, cowardice, the burden of debt, and the domination of men."
"3697","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I entered to Anas ibn Malik after we prayed Zuhr, and his slave girl said to him: Prayer. I said: Which prayer, O Abu Hamzah? He said: Asr. I said: We just prayed Zuhr. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: That is the prayer of the hypocrite; he leaves prayer until when it is at the horn of Satan - or: between the two horns of Satan - he stands and prays, remembering Allah only little."
"3698","Abu Ma'mar Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Hudhali narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abi Namir, from Anas, he said: I never prayed behind an imam lighter in prayer than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3699","Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"3700","Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, the like of it."
"3701","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had supplications he never left: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from anxiety and sorrow, inability and laziness, miserliness and cowardice, the burden of debt, and the domination of men."
"3702","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: I heard Amr, freedman of al-Muttalib, he said: I heard Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: Among the supplication of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he returned with the army: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from anxiety and sorrow, inability and laziness, cowardice and miserliness, the burden of debt, and the domination of men."
"3703","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Amr, freedman of al-Muttalib, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked upon Uhud and said: This is a mountain that loves us and we love it. O Allah, Ibrahim made Makkah sacred, and I make sacred what is between its two lava fields."
"3704","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Amr, freedman of al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, informed me that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Talhah: Seek for us a boy among your boys to serve me. He said: So Abu Talhah took me out, mounting me behind him, and I would serve the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whenever he stopped, and I would hear him often saying: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from anxiety and sorrow, inability and laziness, miserliness and cowardice, the burden of debt, and the domination of men. I continued serving him until we came back from Khaybar, and he came back with Safiyyah bint Huyayy, having taken her, and I would see him making a cushion for her behind him with a cloak or garment, then mounting her behind him. When we were at al-Sahba he made hays in a leather mat, then sent me and I called men, and they ate, and that was his wedding feast with her. Then he went on until Uhud appeared to him, and he said: This is a mountain that loves us and we love it. When he overlooked Madinah, he said: O Allah, I make sacred what is between its two mountains as Ibrahim made Makkah sacred. O Allah, bless them in their mudd and sa'."
"3705","Ahmad ibn Hatim al-Tawil narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Amr informed me, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) chose Safiyyah for himself, until when he reached al-Sahba he consummated with her, then ordered me and I called those around him, and sawiq and dates were brought, and that was the wedding feast of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) making a cushion for her - or: wrapping her - then placing his leg for her so she could mount."
"3706","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Yahya ibn al-Harith, from Amr ibn Amir al-Ansari, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade three things: sacrificial meat beyond three days, visiting graves, and this nabidh in these vessels. Then he said: I forbade you three things, then it occurred to me that people keep their condiments, honor their guests, and store for their absent ones, so eat and keep whatever you wish. I forbade you visiting graves - Abu Bakr doubted, I think - so visit them and do not say foul speech - as if he said: It softens the heart, brings tears to the eye, and reminds of the Hereafter. I forbade you nabidh, so make nabidh in whatever you wish; whoever wishes ties his waterskin upon sin."
"3707","Abu Hammam al-Walid ibn Shuja' narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, with his chain, the like of it."
"3708","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Yahya ibn al-Harith al-Jabir narrated to me, from Abd al-Warith, freedman of Anas, and Amr ibn Amir, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade visiting graves, sacrificial meat after three days, and nabidh in gourds, green jars, and pitch-coated vessels. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said after three: I had forbidden you three things, then it occurred to me about them: I forbade you visiting graves, then it occurred to me that it softens the heart, brings tears to the eye, and reminds of the Hereafter, so visit them and do not say foul speech. I forbade you sacrificial meat lest you eat it beyond three nights, then it occurred to me that people keep their condiments, honor their guests, and store for their absent ones, so keep whatever you wish. I forbade you nabidh in these vessels, so drink in whatever you wish, but do not drink intoxicant; whoever wishes ties his waterskin upon sin."
"3709","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Amr ibn Amir, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform ablution at every prayer. He said: I said: And you, how do you do? He said: We would pray prayers with one ablution as long as we did not break it."
"3710","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Amr, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be cupped, and he would not wrong anyone his wage."
"3711","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Ya'la ibn Ubayd ibn Abi Umayyah narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Amr ibn Amir, he said: I heard Anas saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped, and he would not wrong anyone his wage."
"3712","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Amr, from Anas, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah said: When My servant is tested with his two beloved ones, then is patient, I compensate him for them with Paradise; meaning his two eyes."
"3713","Abu al-Walid al-Qurashi narrated to us, al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Salim informed me that he heard Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Uthman narrating from Anas ibn Malik, that al-Juhani said: O Messenger of Allah, we are where you know, and we cannot attend the month, so inform us of Laylat al-Qadr. He said: Attend the last seven of the month. He said: I cannot do that. He said: Seek it on the seventh night remaining, and it is this night. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the night of twenty-three, which is with eight remaining. He said: Like this, this month decreases, and it is seven remaining."
"3714","Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Abu Dawud, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no wealthy one except he will wish on the Day of Resurrection that what he was given in this world had been mere sustenance."
"3715","Suwayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Isa ibn Abi Isa - who is not al-Aswari - from Anas ibn Malik, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of your condiments is salt."
"3716","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before the Hour there are deceitful years, in which the liar is believed, the truthful denied, the treacherous trusted, and the Ruwaybidah speaks. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the Ruwaybidah? He said: The vile sinner speaking about public affairs."
"3717","Muhammad ibn Jami' al-Attar narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Hammad, from Anas, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"3718","Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, Abu Sahl Yusuf ibn Atiyyah al-Saffar narrated to us, he said: I heard Thabit saying: Anas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of my nation is like rain; it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end."
"3719","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go around all his wives in one night with one bath."
"3720","Abu Sa'id al-Qawariri narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went around his wives in one night with one bath."
"3721","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be straight in your prayer and stand close, for I see you from behind my back. Anas said: I saw one of us join his shoulder to his companion's shoulder, and his foot to his foot, and if you tried to do that today you would see one of them like a refractory mule."
"3722","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten your rows and stand close, for I see you from behind my back."
"3723","Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among the lightest and briefest of people in prayer."
"3724","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Humayd informed us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am in the row in prayer and hear the crying of a child, so I shorten my prayer fearing hardship upon his mother."
"3725","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the voice of a child while in prayer, so he lightened the prayer, and we thought he lightened because his mother was in the prayer."
"3726","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Fajr prayer, then heard a child's crying in the row, and we thought he did that only out of mercy for him."
"3727","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Humayd narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I entered Paradise, and there I was by a river whose banks were tents of pearl. I struck my hand in the course of the water, and it was the most fragrant musk. I said: O Jibril, what is this? He said: This is al-Kawthar which Allah has given you. Or: which your Lord has given you."
"3728","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yahya and Yazid narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a wall belonging to Banu al-Najjar and heard a voice. He said: Who is this? They said: A man who died in ignorance. He said: Were it not that you would not bury one another, I would have asked my Lord to let you hear the punishment of the grave."
"3729","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) vowed abstention from his wives for a month, so he stayed in his upper room with his foot sprained. He said: They entered to him and prayer time came, so he led them sitting, and they prayed standing. Then he came down after twenty-nine, and they said: You vowed a month. He said: The month is twenty-nine."
"3730","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The gray hair on the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not reach twenty hairs."
"3731","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, he raised it: A woman came to him whose son was killed and she had no other than him, and his name was Harithah. She said: O Messenger of Allah, if he is in Paradise I will be patient, and if he is otherwise you will see what I do. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are many gardens, and he is in the highest Firdaws."
"3732","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a she-camel called al-Adba', which was unbeaten. A Bedouin came on a young camel of his and beat her, and it grieved the Muslims. They said: O Messenger of Allah, al-Adba' has been beaten! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is a right upon Allah that nothing of it rises except He lowers it. Meaning this world."
"3733","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, he said: Abu Talhah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have made my garden for Allah, and if I could hide it I would not show it. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give it to the poor among your family."
"3734","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to prayer after it had been called, but a man intercepted him and spoke to him until the people almost dozed."
"3735","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, and Abu Bakr prayed, sitting wrapped in a garment during his illness in which he died."
"3736","Al-Husayn ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to me, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) opened prayer, he would say takbir and raise his hands until his thumbs were level with his ears, then say: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise, blessed is Your name, exalted is Your grandeur, and there is no god but You."
"3737","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni and Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise, and there I was by a palace of gold. I said: Whose palace is this? It was said: For a young man of Quraysh. I thought I was he, so I said: And who is he? It was said: Umar ibn al-Khattab. So by Allah, nothing kept me, O Abu Hafs, from entering it except what I knew of your jealousy. He said: O Messenger of Allah, of whom would I be jealous such that I would not be jealous regarding you? And Hammad said: This is in what people see."
"3738","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas, that he heard him saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Bayda, while I was riding behind Abu Talhah, calling the talbiyah for Hajj and Umrah."
"3739","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had his front tooth broken on the day of Uhud, and was wounded in his forehead until blood flowed over his face. He said: How can a people prosper who did this to their Prophet while he calls them to their Lord? Then this verse was revealed: You have no part in the matter, whether He turns to them or punishes them, for they are wrongdoers."
"3740","Ibn Abi Saminah al-Basri narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas, that the delegation of Thaqif said: O Messenger of Allah, our land is a cold land, so what suffices us of washing from major impurity? He said: As for me, I pour over my head three times."
"3741","Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, from Malik, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruits until they ripen; it was said: what is ripening? He said: until they turn red. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tell me, if Allah withholds the fruit, for what does one of you take his brother's wealth?"
"3742","Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The complexion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brownish."
"3743","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abu Khalid narrated to us, who said: I heard Humayd, from Anas, that Abdullah ibn Salam asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What is the first of the signs of the Hour? He said: Jibril (peace be upon him) informed me that a fire will gather them from the direction of the east."
"3744","Ubaydullah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached to the middle of his ears."
"3745","Abd al-Ala al-Narsi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until it shows ripeness, and selling grapes until they turn black, and selling grain until it hardens."
"3746","Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: The prayer was called, and there was something between the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his wives, and he kept holding some of them back from others, so Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) came and said: Throw dust in their mouths and come out to the prayer."
"3747","Ghassan ibn al-Rabi and Bassam ibn Yazid narrated to us, both said: Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of what you treat yourselves with is cupping, and do not torture your children by pressing the throat for throat swelling."
"3748","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed with a group of his Companions, and there was a small boy on the road, and his mother feared he would be trampled, so she rushed saying: My son, my son, and she took him. The people said: O Messenger of Allah, this woman would never throw her son into the Fire. He said: Nor will Allah throw His beloved into the Fire."
"3749","Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Humayd, from Anas, and he mentioned something similar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3750","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), something similar."
"3751","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: A man would come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) accepting Islam for some worldly thing, accepting it for nothing but that, yet evening would not come before Islam became more beloved to him than the world and what is in it."
"3752","Salih ibn Hatim ibn Wardan narrated to us, al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, who said: I heard Humayd al-Tawil narrating from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed behind Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) in a single garment."
"3753","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raise his hands in bowing and prostration."
"3754","Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Humayd, from Anas, that Umm Sulaym took his hand at the arrival of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madina, and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is Anas, and he is a boy who writes. He said: Anas said: I served him for nine years, and he never said to me for something I did: you did wrong, or: evil is what you did."
"3755","Wahb ibn Baqiyya narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dream of the believer is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"3756","Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was one night praying in his chamber, and some of his Companions came and prayed with his prayer. He said: Then he entered the house, then came out, and returned repeatedly, each time praying. When morning came, they said: O Messenger of Allah, we prayed with you, and we would like you to prolong your prayer. He said: I knew of your place, and I did that deliberately."
"3757","And with the same chain, from Anas, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not admire the deed of anyone until you see how it is sealed for him, for a worker works a period of his life with a righteous deed, such that if he died he would enter Paradise, then he changes and does an evil deed; and a servant works a period of his life with an evil deed, such that if he died he would enter the Fire, then he changes and does a righteous deed; and when Allah wills good for a servant, He employs him before his death. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how does He employ him? He said: He grants him success to a righteous deed, then takes his soul."
"3758","Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: The call to prayer was made, so those whose homes were near the mosque stood and performed ablution, and those who were far from the mosque remained; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a small basin with water in it, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew his fingers together in it due to its narrowness, and the people performed ablution from it. He said: And they were about eighty men."
"3759","Ishaq narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, who said: Anas was asked about the earnings of the cupper, and he did not say about it lawful or unlawful. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped; Abu Tayba cupped him, and he ordered for him two sa of food, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spoke to his family, meaning his owners, and they reduced his tax or his levy, and he said: The best of what you treat yourselves with is cupping and Indian costus, and do not torture your children by pressing the throat."
"3760","Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a man who had become like a plucked chick, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: With what did you supplicate and ask Him? He said: I used to say: O Allah, whatever You will punish me with in the Hereafter, hasten it for me in this world. He said: Glory be to Allah! Can you bear that? Why did you not say: O Allah, Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter and save us from the punishment of the Fire. He said: So he supplicated Allah, and He healed him."
"3761","Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: A funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and they praised it with good, until tongues followed one another with good, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has become due. Then another passed by him and they spoke evil of it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has become due. Then he said: You are the witnesses of Allah on earth."
"3762","Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: I never smelled the scent of musk nor ambergris more pleasant than the scent of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3763","And with his chain: I never touched brocade nor silk softer than the palm of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3764","Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was neither tall nor short; his hair reached to the lobes of his ears, neither curly nor straight."
"3765","Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked, it was as if he was leaning forward."
"3766","Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man of Banu al-Najjar: O uncle, accept Islam. He said: I find myself averse to it. He said: Even if you are averse to it and are compelled to it."
"3767","Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day he set out to Badr consulted the people; he consulted the Muslims, and Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) advised him, and he remained silent; then he consulted, and Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) advised him, so a man of the Ansar said: They only mean you. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we will not say as the Children of Israel said: Go, you and your Lord, and fight; indeed, we are sitting here. But by Allah, if you struck their flanks as far as Barak al-Ghimad, we would be with you."
"3768","And from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was detained from the prayer due to something between his wives, and some of them kept answering back to others, so Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) stood and called out: O Messenger of Allah, throw dust in their mouths and come out to the prayer."
"3769","And from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal is blind in the left eye, with kafir written between his eyes."
"3770","Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit Umm Sulaym and sleep on her bed; he was a heavy sleeper with much sweat, and she would take his sweat with a piece of cotton and put it in a bottle, and place it in a perfume container she had."
"3771","And from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out one day with his head bandaged, and men of the Ansar met him, and he said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I love you. The Ansar have fulfilled what was upon them, and what remains is upon you; so accept from their doers of good and overlook their offenders."
"3772","And from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not hate one another, do not envy one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and be, O servants of Allah, brothers."
"3773","Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Humayd, from Anas, that Thabit ibn Qays addressed at the arrival of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: We will protect you from what we protect ourselves and our children from; so what is for us, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Paradise is for you. They said: We are pleased."
"3774","And from Anas, that the Muhajirun came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we never saw people more generous with much, nor better in sharing little, than the Ansar; we came to Madina and they shared with us the pleasant life; we fear they will take the reward. He said: No, as long as you praise them and supplicate for them."
"3775","And from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with one of his wives, and another sent to him a bowl with food in it; when the one in whose house he was came, she struck the hand of the servant, and the bowl fell and broke. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it and kept putting the food back into it, saying: Your mother felt jealous. When she brought her bowl, he took it and sent it to the one whose bowl was broken."
"3776","Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Humayd, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: A morning march in the path of Allah is better than the world and what is in it, and the space of a bow of one of you in Paradise is better than the world and what is in it; and if a woman of the women of Paradise were to look down to the earth, she would fill what is between them with the scent of musk, and she would illuminate what is between them, and her head-cover is better than the world and what is in it."
"3777","And from Anas, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Give me a mount. He said: We shall mount you on the offspring of a she-camel. He said: What shall I do with the offspring of a she-camel? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And do she-camels give birth to anything but camels."
"3778","And from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from Khaybar until, when between Madina and Khaybar, he consummated marriage with Safiyya; he stayed with her three days and gave a feast; Umm Sulaym baked bread, spread a leather mat, and they poured into it dates, ghee and dried yogurt, and there was nothing else; then he mounted, and the people said: If he veils her, she is of the Mothers of the Believers. When he mounted, he carried her with him and veiled her with a garment; and when he entered Madina he would hasten his camel and urge his mount; when he entered, he hastened his camel, and the people climbed up, and the Mothers of the Believers were looking at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and at her, and the she-camel stumbled, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell, and he had no concern except to arrange her clothes upon her. He said: It was as if they gloated over her."
"3779","Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Humayd, from Anas, that Abu Talha used to shoot arrows in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he would raise his head to look at the spot of his arrow, then he raised it and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his, so Abu Talha raised his chest opposite him and said: Like this, O Messenger of Allah, may Allah make me your ransom."
"3780","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Ali ibn Zayd informed us from Anas, who said: I attended the wedding feast of two of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they did not feed us bread nor meat. He said: I said: Then what? He said: Hays (a mixture of dates, ghee and dried yogurt)."
"3781","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Muadh ibn Muadh al-Anbari narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Muhajirun said: O Messenger of Allah, we never saw the like of a people we came to, better in giving from much, nor better in sharing from little; they have sufficed us the burden and shared with us the pleasant life, and we fear they will take all the reward. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, as long as you praise them and supplicate Allah for them."
"3782","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Muadh ibn Muadh narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf came as an emigrant, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood between him and Sad ibn al-Rabi; Sad said to him: I have wealth, half of it is yours, and I have two wives, so look at whichever of them is more beloved to you and I shall divorce her, and when her waiting period ends you shall marry her. Abd al-Rahman said to him: May Allah bless you in your family and wealth; show me the market. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed him for days, then he came to him with traces of yellow perfume on him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What is this? He said: I married a woman of the Ansar. He said: What did you give her as dowry? He said: A date-stone weight of gold, or: the weight of a date-stone of gold. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give a feast even with a sheep."
"3783","Sufyan ibn Waki narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that Abdullah ibn Salam asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the first of the signs of the Hour, and he said: Jibril informed me that a fire will gather them from the east."
"3784","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abd al-Qahir ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Seventy thousand of my community will enter Paradise. They said: Increase for us, O Messenger of Allah. He said: For each man, seventy thousand. They said: Increase for us, O Messenger of Allah. He was on a sand dune, and he scooped with his hand. They said: Increase for us, O Messenger of Allah. He said: This, and he scooped with his hand. They said: O Prophet of Allah, may Allah keep far from the Fire whoever enters after this."
"3785","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: There was no person in the world whose sight was more beloved to them than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), yet when they saw him they would not stand for him, because of what they knew of his dislike for that."
"3786","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, that Anas was asked about the hair of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: The hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not go beyond his ears, as if it were the hair of Qatada. Qatada rejoiced that day, and the hair of Qatada was wavy."
"3787","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Qudama ibn Shihab narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered a house, or a place, and saw a rope stretched out, and said: What is this? They said: So-and-so woman prays; when she tires she holds it. He said: Let her pray, and when she tires let her sleep, or let her sit."
"3788","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at al-Baqi, and a man called: O Abu al-Qasim. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned, and the man said: I did not mean you. He said: Name yourselves with my name but do not use my kunya."
"3789","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit and Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I certainly gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to drink honey, nabidh, water and milk in this very cup."
"3790","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Nafi narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the virgin, seven days, and for the previously married, three."
"3791","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Umayr narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When the wind blew, that would be recognized on the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3792","Abu Said al-Ashajj narrated to us, al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Sallam ibn Sulaym, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The period of postnatal bleeding is forty days, unless she sees purity before that."
"3793","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Husayn al-Jufi narrated to us, from Zaida, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: I never saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray Maghrib until he broke his fast, even if with a sip of water."
"3794","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raising his hands when he began the prayer, when he bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing."
"3795","Harun al-Hammal narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Humayd informed us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you has fever, let him sprinkle cold water upon himself for three nights before dawn."
"3796","Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that there was something between the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he kept forbidding them, and he was detained from the prayer, so Abu Bakr called to him: O Messenger of Allah, throw dust in their faces and come out to the prayer."
"3797","Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up one of his wives and measured a span or two spans from her hem, and said: Do not exceed this."
"3798","Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, who said: I heard Humayd narrating from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: No servant dies, having good with Allah, who loves to return to the world with the world and what is in it for him, except the martyr, due to what he sees of the virtue of martyrdom; he loves to return to the world and be killed again."
"3799","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, who said: I heard Humayd, and he mentioned that he heard Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out one day with his head bandaged, and the Ansar met him with their faces and their youths, and he said: By the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, I love you. The Ansar have fulfilled what was upon them, and what remains is upon you; so do good to their doers of good and overlook their offenders."
"3800","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, who said: I heard Humayd narrating from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: None of you should wish for death due to harm that has befallen him in the world, but let him say: O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is better for me, and take my soul when death is better for me."
"3801","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, who said: I heard Humayd who said: Anas was asked: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) take a ring? He said: Yes, as if I am looking at the glitter of his ring. One night he delayed the last Isha prayer until midnight, then prayed; when he finished his prayer he turned to us with his face and said: The people have prayed and slept, and you will remain in prayer as long as you wait for it. He said: As if I am looking at the glitter of his ring. He said: His ring was of silver, its stone of it."
"3802","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, who said: I heard Humayd narrating from Anas, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about the time of the Fajr prayer. When we woke the next morning, he ordered when dawn broke that the prayer be established. The next day he delayed it until it was bright, then ordered and the prayer was established, and he prayed with us, then said: Where is the questioner about the time of prayer? What is between these two is the time."
"3803","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, I heard Humayd narrating from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: He visited a Muslim man, entering upon him while he was like a plucked chick from exertion, and said: Did you supplicate with something and ask Him? He said: Yes, I used to say: O Allah, whatever You will punish me with in the Hereafter, hasten it for me in this world. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glory be to Allah! You cannot bear it, or: you are not able to. Why did you not say: O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter and save us from the punishment of the Fire. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for him, and Allah the Mighty and Majestic healed him."
"3804","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, who said: I heard Humayd narrating from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one day and marched to Badr, consulting the people; Abu Bakr advised him, then he consulted them, and Umar advised him, and he kept consulting, so the Ansar said: By Allah, he wants none but us. A man of the Ansar said: I see you consult and they advise you, but we will not say as the Children of Israel said: Go, you and your Lord, and fight. Rather, by the One Who sent you with the truth, if you struck their flanks until you reach al-Ghimad, we would be with you."
"3805","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raided a people, he would not raid until morning; he would look, and if he heard the call to prayer he refrained from them, and if he did not hear the call he attacked them. He said: So we set out to Khaybar and reached it; in the morning he heard no call, so he mounted and I rode behind Abu Talha, and my foot touched the foot of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: They came out to us with their baskets and shovels; when they saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they said: Muhammad and the army. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw them, he said: Allah is Greatest, Khaybar is ruined; when we descend in the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those warned."
"3806","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, who said: I heard Humayd narrating from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I was at his right or left thigh: Here I am for Umra and Hajj."
"3807","And from Anas, who said: We traveled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and neither did a fasting person criticize one breaking fast, nor one breaking fast criticize a fasting person. The people were exhausted one day in Ramadan while traveling, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a vessel and drank it so the people would see that he was breaking fast."
"3808","And from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey of his in Ramadan while fasting, and he was brought a vessel of water; he placed it on his hand and drank it, with the people looking, and they drank."
"3809","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, who said: I heard Humayd narrating from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he stood at night over the well in which were Abu Jahl and his companions at Badr, three days after their killing, and called: O Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, O Utba ibn Rabia, O Shayba ibn Rabia, O Umayya ibn Khalaf, did you find what your Lord promised you to be true? I have found what my Lord promised me to be true. He said: Those of his Companions whom Allah willed came out to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, do you call a people who have decayed for three days? He said: You are not better hearers of what I say than they, except that they cannot answer me."
"3810","Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked over the well, and he mentioned something similar."
"3811","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal al-Darir narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: While a man was driving a sacrificial camel, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Ride it even if it is a sacrificial camel."
"3812","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Baqi al-Gharqad, and a man was calling his companion: O Abu al-Qasim! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned, and he said: I did not mean you, O Messenger of Allah, I only meant so-and-so. He said: Name yourselves with my name but do not use my kunya."
"3813","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dream of the believer is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"3814","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, a man peeked at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through a crack, and he aimed at him with a broad arrowhead."
"3815","Masruq ibn al-Marzuban narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to the prayer, let him walk calmly; let him pray what he catches and make up what he missed."
"3816","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divorced Hafsa, he was commanded to take her back, so he took her back."
"3817","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved that the Muhajirun and Ansar be next to him so they would learn from him."
"3818","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was close, one to another; the prayer of Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) was similar; then Umar extended the morning prayer."
"3819","And from Anas, that a morsel fell from his hand and he sought it until he found it, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the morsel of one of you falls, let him remove harm from it and eat it, and not leave it for Satan."
"3820","And from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fast part of the month until we would say: he does not break fast; and he would break fast until we would say: he does not fast anything of it."
"3821","And from Anas, that the Ansar had two days in which they played in the pre-Islamic period; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived, he said: Allah has replaced for you two days better than them: al-Fitr and al-Adha."
"3822","And from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah wills good for a servant, He employs him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how does He employ him? He said: He grants him success so he does a righteous deed before his death."
"3823","And from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and heard a movement before me. She said: I am al-Ghumaysa bint Milhan."
"3824","And from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and there I was at a flowing river whose banks were tents of pearl. He said: I struck my hand into the clay and it was strong-smelling musk. I said: O Jibril, what is this? He said: This is al-Kawthar which Allah gave you."
"3825","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Muadh ibn Muadh narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: When Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf came as an emigrant to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he established brotherhood between him and Sad ibn al-Rabi; Sad said to him: I have wealth, half of it is yours, and I have two wives, so look at whichever of them is more beloved to you and I shall divorce her, and when her waiting period ends you shall marry her. Abd al-Rahman said to him: May Allah bless you in your family and wealth; show me the market. He did not return that day until he came with something he had gained from the market. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed him for days, then he came to him with traces of yellow perfume on him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What is this? He said: I married a woman of the Ansar. He said: What dowry did you give from her? He said: A date-stone of gold, or he said: the weight of a date-stone of gold. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Give a feast even with a sheep."
"3826","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) swore off his wives for a month; he stayed in an upper room of his, and his foot was dislocated; his Companions came to visit him, and he prayed with them sitting while they were standing; then they came for another prayer and he sat while they stood, so he gestured to them to sit, and they prayed behind him sitting; when twenty-nine nights had passed, he came down to them, and it was said: O Messenger of Allah, only twenty-nine nights have passed! He said: The month is twenty-nine."
"3827","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit and Humayd, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions used to pray toward Bayt al-Maqdis; when this verse was revealed: Turn your face toward al-Masjid al-Haram, a man of Banu Salima passed and called to them while they were bowing in the Fajr prayer toward Bayt al-Maqdis: Indeed the qibla has been changed. So they turned as they were, bowing, toward the qibla."
"3828","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring of silver, its stone of it."
"3829","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fast the month until we would say: he does not break fast; and he would break fast the month until we would say: he does not fast."
"3830","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man works a period of his life with the deed of the people of Paradise, then before his death he changes and works with the deed of the people of the Fire, and dies and enters the Fire; and a man works a period of his life with the deed of the people of the Fire, then before his death he works with the deed of the people of Paradise, and dies and enters Paradise."
"3831","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Qatada, Thabit and Humayd, from Anas, who said: Prices rose in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they said: O Messenger of Allah, prices have risen, so fix prices for us. He said: Allah is the One Who fixes prices, the Withholder, the Extender, the Provider; I hope to meet Allah with none of you seeking me for an injustice in blood or wealth."
"3832","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, and Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a rope stretched between two pillars in the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is this rope? It was said: O Messenger of Allah, Hamna bint Jahsh prays; when she tires she holds on. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let her pray, and when she tires let her sit."
"3833","Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was of medium stature, of good body, neither tall nor short; his hair was neither curly nor straight, brownish in color; when he walked he leaned forward."
"3834","Abu Yusuf al-Jizi narrated to us, Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Persist with: O Possessor of Majesty and Honor."
"3835","Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, the Prophet married Safiyya and made her freedom her dowry, and made the feast three days; a leather mat brought by Umm Sulaym was spread, and dried yogurt and dates were placed upon it, and he fed the people three days."
"3836","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas, that Abu Musa asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a mount and found him busy, so he swore he would not carry me. He said: And I swear I shall carry you. So he carried him."
"3837","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Humayd informed us, from Anas, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf emigrated to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood between him and Sad ibn al-Rabi; Sad ibn al-Rabi said to him: O Abd al-Rahman, I am among the wealthiest of the Ansar, and I shall share with you; I have two wives, and I shall divorce one of them for you, and when her waiting period ends marry her. Abd al-Rahman said to him: May Allah bless you in your family and wealth; rather show me the market. He showed him, and he did not return that day until he had gained some ghee and dried yogurt as profit. He stayed days, then passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he saw traces of yellow perfume. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What is this? He said: I married, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Whom? He said: A woman of the Ansar. He said: What dowry did you give? He said: A date-stone, or the weight of a date-stone, of gold. He said: Give a feast even with a sheep."
"3838","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited a man who had become like a plucked chick, and said: Did you supplicate with something, or ask Him? He said: I said: O Allah, whatever You will punish me with in the Hereafter, hasten it for me in this world. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Glory be to Allah! Then you cannot bear that, nor are you able to. Why did you not say: Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter and save us from the punishment of the Fire."
"3839","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, from al-Hasan, and Humayd informed us, from Anas, both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Help your brother, oppressor or oppressed. They said: O Messenger of Allah, this one we help oppressed; how do we help him oppressing? He said: You prevent him from oppression."
"3840","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid informed us, Humayd informed us, from Anas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from the expedition of Tabuk and neared Madina, he said: In Madina there are peoples; you did not travel a journey nor cross a valley but they were with you in it. They said: O Messenger of Allah, while they are in Madina? He said: Yes, excuse detained them."
"3841","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You need not admire anyone until you see how it is sealed for him, for a worker works a period of his life, or a portion of his time, with a righteous deed such that if he died upon it he would enter Paradise, then he changes and works an evil deed; and a servant works a period of his life with an evil deed such that if he died upon it he would enter the Fire, then he changes and works a righteous deed; and when Allah wills good for a servant, He employs him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how does He employ him? He said: He grants him success to a righteous deed, then takes his soul upon it."
"3842","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Humayd informed us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Madina, and they had two days in which they played. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have come to you and you have two days in which you play, and Allah has replaced for you two days better than them: the day of Fitr and the day of Sacrifice."
"3843","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man being supported between his two sons, and said: What is this? They said: He vowed to walk to the House. He said: Allah is in no need of this one torturing himself. Then he ordered him and he rode."
"3844","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque and saw a rope stretched between two pillars, and said: What is this? They said: It belongs to so-and-so woman; she prays, and when she tires she holds onto it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let her pray as long as she is mindful; when she fears being overcome, let her sleep."
"3845","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas, who said: The prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr was similar, until Umar came and extended the dawn prayer."
"3846","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A people will come who are more tender-hearted than you. The Asharis came, among them Abu Musa, and they began chanting, saying:"
"3847","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Humayd informed us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal is with the eye wiped out, over it a thick membrane; written between his eyes is k f r."
"3848","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should wish for death due to harm that has befallen him, but let him say: O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is better for me, and take my soul when You know death is better for me."
"3849","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Humayd informed us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved that the Muhajirun and Ansar be next to him in prayer so they would learn from him."
"3850","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Humayd informed us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in one of the houses of his wives, and a wife of his gifted the Prophet a bowl of tharid; she struck it with her hand, and it fell and the bowl broke. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began taking the tharid with his hand and putting it back into the bowl, saying: Eat, your mother felt jealous. Then he waited until the other bowl came, took it and gave it to the owner of the broken bowl."
"3851","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped by Abu Tayba; he ordered for him two sa of food, spoke to his owners and they reduced his levy, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of what you treat yourselves with is cupping and Indian costus, and do not torture your children by pressing the throat for throat swelling."
"3852","And from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until it ripens. We said: What is its ripening? He said: It turns red. Anas said: Tell me, if Allah withholds the palm trees, with what do you deem lawful the wealth of your brother?"
"3853","And from Anas ibn Malik: We never wished to see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at night praying but we saw him, and we never wished to see him at night sleeping but we saw him sleeping."
"3854","And from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque and saw sputum on its front wall, and the severity of that was seen upon him. He said: When one of you stands to pray, he stands conversing privately with his Lord, or: his Lord is between him and the qibla. When one of you spits, let him spit to his left under his foot, or spit like this. And he spat in the edge of his cloak and rubbed part of it with part."
"3855","And from Anas ibn Malik, who said: A funeral was brought past the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they praised it with good, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has become due. Then another funeral was brought past, and they spoke evil of it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It has become due. You are the witnesses of Allah on earth."
"3856","Zuhayr informed us, Yazid narrated to us, Yahya and Humayd informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the best quarters of the Ansar? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The quarters of Banu al-Najjar, then the quarters of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, then the quarters of Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, then the quarters of Banu Saida. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And in every quarter of the Ansar there is good. One of them said: And he raised his voice with it."
"3857","Zuhayr informed us, Yazid narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, that Abdullah ibn Salam came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I shall ask you about three things which none knows but a prophet. He said: Ask. He said: What is the first matter of the Hour, or the signs of the Hour? What is the first food the people of Paradise eat? And what makes the child resemble his father, and the child his mother? He said: Jibril informed me of them just now. He said: Jibril? He said: Yes. He said: He is the enemy of the Jews among the angels. He said: As for the first of the signs of the Hour, it is a fire that comes out from the east and gathers the people to the west. As for the first food the people of Paradise eat, it is the extra lobe of the fish liver. As for what makes the child resemble his father and the child his mother, when the fluid of the man precedes the fluid of the woman, it resembles his father, and when the fluid of the woman precedes the fluid of the man, it resembles his mother. He said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, the Jews are a slanderous people; I shall hide from them, then ask them about me, before they know of my Islam, what kind of man I am among them. A group of them came, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: What kind of man is Abdullah among you? They said: Our best and the son of our best, our chief and the son of our chief, our most knowledgeable and the son of our most knowledgeable. He said: What if Abdullah accepts Islam? They said: May Allah protect him from that. Abdullah came out to them and said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. They said: Our worst and the son of our worst, and similar. Abdullah says: O Messenger of Allah, this is what I feared."
"3858","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Humayd informed us, from Anas, that the Muslims heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, O Umayya ibn Khalaf, O Utba ibn Rabia, O Shayba ibn Rabia, did you find what your Lord promised you to be true? I have found what my Lord promised me to be true. They said: O Messenger of Allah, do you call a people who have decayed? He said: You are not better hearers of what I say than they, but they cannot answer."
"3859","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Humayd informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that after the prayer was established and before he said the takbir, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to the people with his face and said: Straighten your rows and stand close together, for I see you from behind my back. He said: I would see a man in the row joining his shoulder to his companion's shoulder."
"3860","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one night in his chamber, and the people heard his voice; the second night people came and prayed with his prayer, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shortened, then left. In the morning they said: O Messenger of Allah, we prayed with you last night, and we would like you to prolong your recitation. He said: I knew of your place, and I did that deliberately."
"3861","And from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and saw a palace of gold. I said: Whose is this? They said: For a youth of Quraysh. I thought I was he, so I said: For whom? It was said: For Umar ibn al-Khattab."
"3862","And from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a wedding feast for Zaynab, feeding the Muslims bread and meat to their fill; then he went out as he used to do when he married, visiting the chambers of the Mothers of the Believers, greeting them and supplicating for them, and they greeting him and supplicating for him; then he returned and there were two men in the house deep in conversation. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw them, he turned back; when the two men saw that, they jumped up startled and left. I do not know who informed him; I informed him or another; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned."
"3863","And from Anas, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the time of the Fajr prayer, so he ordered Bilal, who called the adhan for Fajr, then established it and he prayed. The next day he delayed until it was bright, then ordered him and he established it and he prayed. When he finished, he said: Where is the questioner? The man stood, and he said: What is between this and this is the time."
"3864","He said: Anas was asked: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raise his hands in supplication? He said: Yes. While he was one Friday addressing the people, it was said: O Messenger of Allah, rain has ceased, the land is barren, wealth has perished, so supplicate Allah. He said: He raised his hands until I saw the whiteness of his armpits, and prayed for rain, and I saw no cloud in the sky. We had not finished the prayer before even a youth near his home was concerned about returning to his family. It lasted a week; the second Friday they said: O Messenger of Allah, houses have collapsed, riders are detained, wealth has perished. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled, then gestured with his hand, parting between them, then said: O Allah, around us and not upon us, separating between his hands. He said: It was cleared away from Madina."
"3865","And from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in his house, and a man peeked through the door, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) aimed at him with a broad arrowhead, and the man drew back."
"3866","And from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When: You will never attain righteousness until you spend of what you love was revealed, or: Who is it that will lend Allah a good loan, Abu Talha said: O Messenger of Allah, my garden at such-and-such place is for Allah; had I been able to conceal it I would not have announced it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Put it among your relatives. Or he said: Among your kin."
"3867","And from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I never smelled a scent, musk or perfume, more pleasant than the scent of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor did I touch brocade or silk softer than the palm of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3868","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Habban ibn Hilal narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combining watermelon with fresh dates."
"3869","Abu Khaythama narrated to us, Habban narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salama, from Humayd and Thabit, from Anas, who said: I gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to drink water, milk, nabidh and honey in this cup."
"3870","Zuhayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed a man driving a sacrificial camel, and said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel. He said: Ride it."
"3871","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who was asked about the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: I never saw hair more like the hair of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than the hair of Qatada. Qatada rejoiced that day."
"3872","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Qatada, Humayd and Thabit informed us, from Anas, that some people of Urayna came to Madina and found its climate unhealthy; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent them out to the camels of charity, saying: Drink their urine and milk. They killed the shepherd of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), drove off the camels and apostatized from Islam. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had them brought, cut off their hands and feet on opposite sides, branded their eyes, and cast them in al-Harra. Anas said: I would see one of them biting the ground with his mouth until they died; sometimes Hammad said: biting the ground with his mouth until they died."
"3873","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, similar to the hadith of Hammad; and Hammam mentioned that Qatada said: Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to me that this was before the hudud punishments were revealed."
"3874","Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Tamimi al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon a sick person, he would say: Remove the harm, Lord of mankind; heal, You are the Healer; there is no healer but You; heal a healing that leaves no illness. And Hammad said: There is no healing but Your healing; heal a healing that leaves no illness."
"3875","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Qatada, Thabit and Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman used to begin the prayer with: All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds. And Humayd would not mention the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3876","Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Strive against the polytheists with your hands and your tongues."
"3877","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for prayer, and a man came after the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had stood, hastening his walk; he reached the people breathless, or breath overcame him. When he reached the row he said: Praise be to Allah, much good blessed praise. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer, he said: Who is the speaker, or: the sayer of the words. The people fell silent, so he said the like. He said: Who is he? He said nothing wrong, or: he said good. The man said: I came, O Messenger of Allah, hastening my walk; I reached the row breathless, or breath overcame me, so I said what I said. He said: I saw twelve angels racing to it, which of them would raise it to Him. Then he said: When one of you comes to the prayer, let him walk calmly; let him pray what he catches and make up what he missed."
"3878","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, Abu Wahb said: I know not but he mentioned it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him; whoever hates to meet Allah, Allah hates to meet him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, all of us hate death. He said: It is not hatred of death, but when the glad tidings come to him from Allah of what he is heading to, he loves to meet Allah, and Allah loves to meet him; and the disbeliever, or: the wicked, when attended, what he shall face comes to him, and he hates to meet Allah, and Allah hates to meet him."
"3879","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Umm Sulaym, and she brought him ghee and dates. He said: Put your ghee back in its skin and your dates in their container, for I am fasting. Then he stood and prayed a prayer not obligatory, and we prayed; he supplicated for Umm Sulaym and her household. Umm Sulaym said: I have a dear one. He said: What is she? She said: Your servant Anas. He said: So he supplicated for me with the good of this world and the Hereafter, saying: O Allah, grant him wealth and children and bless him in it. He said: I am among the Ansar with most children. He said: Umayna informed me that over a hundred and twenty of my progeny were buried up to the arrival of al-Hajjaj in Basra."
"3880","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man of Banu al-Najjar: Accept Islam. He said: I find myself averse. He said: Accept Islam even if you are averse."
"3881","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: A man would ask the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for something of the world and accept Islam for it; then evening would not come before Islam became more beloved to him than the world and what is in it."
"3882","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he saw an old man being supported between his two sons. They said: O Messenger of Allah, he vowed to walk. He said: Allah is in no need of this one torturing himself. Then he ordered him and he rode."
"3883","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, who said: A son of Abu Talha fell ill, and he went to the mosque, and the boy died; Umm Sulaym arranged her household, prepared his dinner, and said to her family: Let none of you mention the death of his son to Abu Talha. Abu Talha returned with some of his companions of the people of the mosque, and said: How is the boy? Umm Sulaym said: In the best state he was. She served his dinner, and he and his companions ate; when they left him, she rose to what a woman rises to. At the end of the night she said: Did you not see, O Abu Talha, the family of so-and-so! They borrowed a loan, enjoyed it, and when it was sought from them, it grieved them! He said: They were not just. She said: So-and-so, her son, was a loan from Allah, and He took it back. He declared return to Allah. Then he went in the morning to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: May Allah bless you both in your night. She conceived Abdullah. When she gave birth at night, she disliked having him chewed for until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) chewed for him. He said: I went with him in the morning with Ajwa dates, coming to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was tarring his camels and branding them. I said: O Messenger of Allah, Umm Sulaym gave birth last night, and she disliked having him chewed for until you chew for him. He said: Is there something with you? I said: Ajwa dates. He took some of those dates, chewed them, gathered his saliva and fed it to him; the boy smacked his lips. He said: The beloved of the Ansar is dates. I said: Name him, O Messenger of Allah. He said: He is Abdullah."
"3884","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ibrahim al-Talqani narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived from a journey and saw the walls of Madina, he hastened his she-camel; if he was on a mount he urged it, out of love for it."
"3885","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, and Abu Bakr prayed sitting, wrapped in his garment, during his illness in which he died."
"3886","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out for the prayer when the iqamah for the prayer had already been made, then a man met him and spoke to him, until the people almost dozed off."
"3887","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went around to his wives in one night with a single ritual bath."
"3888","Zuhayr narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf married for a date-stone's weight - or the weight of a date-stone - of gold, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Hold a wedding feast, even if with a sheep."
"3889","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a man perfume himself with saffron."
"3890","Abu al-Rabi al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a man perfume himself with saffron."
"3891","Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah and made her emancipation her dowry."
"3892","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should wish for death because of a harm that has befallen him, and if he must wish, let him say: O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is good for me, and cause me to die when death is good for me."
"3893","Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Shubah informed us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer should not wish for death because of a harm that has befallen him, and if he must do so, let him say: O Allah, keep me alive as long as life is good for me, and cause me to die when death is good for me."
"3894","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, who said: Qatadah asked Anas: Which supplication did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) make most often? He said: The supplication the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made most often was that he would say: O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter and shield us from the punishment of the Fire. He said: And when Anas wanted to make a supplication he would supplicate with it, and when he wanted to make a dua he would make dua with it."
"3895","Jafar ibn Mihran narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from extreme old age, and I seek refuge in You from cowardice, and I seek refuge in You from miserliness, and I seek refuge in You from laziness."
"3896","Jafar narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant truly believes until I am more beloved to him than his family, his wealth, and all people together."
"3897","Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring of gold and engraved on it: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah, and he forbade engraving after his engraving."
"3898","Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray briefly and completely."
"3899","Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray briefly and completely."
"3900","Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Muadh. He said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Give glad tidings to the people that whoever says: There is no god but Allah, will enter Paradise."
"3901","Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."
"3902","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah and Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat the pre-dawn meal, for in the pre-dawn meal there is blessing."
"3903","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, Anas narrated to us, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered the lavatory, would say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from male and female devils."
"3904","Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, who said: I was serving my paternal uncles fadikh made from unripe dates when we heard a caller calling: Verily wine has been forbidden. He said: So they said: Pour it away, O Anas. He said: By Allah, they did not say: Let us wait and look and ask. He said: And fadikh was at that time among their wines. He said: And he mentioned among those who were there that day Abu Talhah and Suhayl ibn Bayda and people from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3905","Zahmawayh narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"3906","Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Anas, who said: People from Uraynah came to Madinah and found its climate unhealthy, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: If you wish, go out to the charity camels and drink from their urine and their milk. He said: So they did, and they recovered. Then they attacked the herdsmen, killed them, drove away the camels of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and disbelieved after their Islam. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent men after them, and they were brought, and he cut off their hands and feet, branded their eyes, and left them in the lava field until they died."
"3907","Zahmawayh narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, who said: I sought the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day, and it was said to me: He is with a tailor of the family of al-Muttalib; he invited him and he accepted. So I went until I entered upon him, and the tailor had prepared food in which there was pumpkin, so I began taking the pumpkin and placing it before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), because of what I knew of his love for it."
"3908","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Mubarak the freedman of Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The parable of my nation is like a river from which one bathes five times; what filth can remain upon him? He stands for ablution and washes his hands, so every sin his hands touched falls away, and he rinses his mouth, so every sin his tongue spoke falls away, then he washes his face, so every sin his eyes looked at falls away, then he wipes his head, so every sin his ears heard falls away, then he washes his feet, so every sin his feet walked to falls away."
"3909","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Mubarak narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be people in my nation who will shoot out of the religion as the arrow shoots out of the game; they are the worst of those killed under the shadow of the sky. Glad tidings to whoever kills them; glad tidings to whomever they kill; glad tidings to whomever they kill."
"3910","Al-Muqaddami narrated to us, from Mubarak, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the believer. He said: The one whose neighbor feels safe from him and does not fear his treacheries; and the Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand people are safe."
"3911","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Mubarak narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the worst of you? They said: Yes. He said: The worst of you are those whose evil is feared and whose good is not hoped for; and the best of you are those whose good is hoped for and whose evil is not feared."
"3912","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, I heard Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrating, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things will remain in my nation until the Hour comes: wailing over the dead, boasting about lineages, and seeking rain by the stars."
"3913","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things will never cease in my nation, and he mentioned something similar."
"3914","Jafar ibn Mihran narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Emigrants and the Helpers were digging the trench around Madinah and carrying the soil on their backs, and saying - He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would answer them while replying to them: The Helpers and the Emigrants. He said: And two handfuls of barley would be brought to them, and it would be prepared for them with rancid melted fat, which was unpleasant in the throat and had a foul odor, and it would be placed before the people."
"3915","Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Shubah and Hammad ibn Salamah and Hushaym informed us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he entered the lavatory he would say: I seek refuge in You from male and female devils."
"3916","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, with the like of it."
"3917","Ja'far ibn Mihran narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent seventy men for a need, called the Qurra', and two clans of Banu Sulaym, Ri'l and Dhakwan, confronted them at a well called Bi'r Ma'unah. The people said: By Allah, we did not intend you; we are only passing through on a need for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So they killed them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated against them for a month in the dawn prayer; that was the beginning of qunut, and we had not used to perform qunut."
"3918","Ja'far ibn Mihran narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, who said: Thabit and I entered upon Anas, and Thabit said to him: O Abu Hamzah, I have fallen ill. So Anas ibn Malik said to him: Shall I not charm you with the ruqyah of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes indeed. O Allah, Lord of mankind, remove the harm, heal, You are the Healer, there is no healer but You, a healing that leaves no sickness."
"3919","Ja'far narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) consummated his marriage with Zaynab bint Jahsh and served food over her, holding a wedding feast of bread and meat. He said: So I was sent, and the food was covered, and I invited people; a group would come and eat, then leave, and I kept inviting until I could not find anyone to invite. I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I cannot find anyone to invite. He said: Then lift up your food. And Zaynab was sitting in the side of the house. He said: She was a woman who had been given beauty, and three men remained in the house talking, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and headed toward A'ishah's chamber, and said: Peace be upon you, people of the house, and the mercy of Allah; how have you woken this morning? She said: And upon you, and the mercy of Allah; how did you find your wife? May Allah bless you in them. He said: So he visited all the chambers of his wives in turn, saying to them as he had said to A'ishah, and they said to him as A'ishah had said. Then the Prophet of Allah returned and there were the three men talking in the house, and the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was intensely shy, so he headed back toward A'ishah's chamber, and I do not know whether I informed him or he was informed that the people had left, so he returned, and when he had placed one of his feet in the threshold of the door and the other outside, he lowered a curtain between me and him, and the verse of hijab was revealed."
"3920","Ja'far narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas, who said: A man was a Christian and became Muslim in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he read al-Baqarah and Al Imran. He said: And he used to write for the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Then he went back to being a Christian and used to say: I do not see that Muhammad does well except what I used to write for him. So Allah caused him to die and they buried him, and in the morning the earth had cast him out. They said: This is the deed of Muhammad and his companions; because he was not pleased with their religion, they dug up our companion and threw him out. He said: So they dug a grave for him and made it deep, and in the morning the earth had cast him out. They said: This is the deed of Muhammad and his companions; they dug up our companion and threw him out. He said: So they dug a grave for him and went as deep into the earth as they could, and in the morning the earth had cast him out, so they knew that it was not from men and that it was from Allah, Mighty and Majestic, so they cast him away."
"3921","Ja'far narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to prayer, and a man confronted him and said: O Messenger of Allah, when will the Hour come? He said: And what have you prepared for it? He said: Nothing except that I love Allah and His Messenger. He said: Then you will be with those you love. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer, he said: Where is the one who asked about the Hour? He said: So he came and stood, and he said: O you. Anas said: And a boy of Daws, he and I the same age. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If this boy lives long and does not die in old age before the Hour comes."
"3922","Ja'far narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, who said: On the day of Uhud, people fled from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while Abu Talhah was in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shielding him with a leather shield he had with him. He said: And Abu Talhah was a strong archer with a powerful draw; on that day he broke two or three bows. A man would pass with a quiver containing arrows, and he would say: Scatter them for Abu Talhah. He said: And the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would raise his head to look at the people, and Abu Talhah would say: O Prophet of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, do not raise your head lest an arrow of the enemy strike you; my neck is before your neck. And I saw A'ishah bint Abi Bakr and Umm Sulaym, and they had tucked up their garments, I could see the anklets of their shanks, carrying water on their backs, then pouring it into the mouths of the people, then returning to fill them, then coming back and pouring it into the mouths of the people. And the sword fell from Abu Talhah's hand out of drowsiness, either twice or three times."
"3923","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat sahur, for there is blessing in sahur."
"3924","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, who said: I heard Anas saying: Eat sahur, for there is blessing in sahur."
"3925","Ja'far ibn Mihran narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not come out to us for three days, and the prayer was established, so Abu Bakr went forward to lead, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said of the curtain: lift it. When the whiteness of the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became clear to us, we never looked upon a sight more pleasing to us than the face of the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when it became clear to us. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to Abu Bakr to go forward. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) let down the curtain, and we could not see him again until he died."
"3926","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Umarah narrated to us, who said: I heard Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to perfume his skin with saffron."
"3927","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Shu'bah informed us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb informed us, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik mention the marriage of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Safiyyah. Thabit said: What did he give her as dowry? Anas said: He gave her herself as dowry; he freed her and married her."
"3928","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has three children die before reaching the age of discernment, Allah will admit him to Paradise by virtue of His mercy upon them."
"3929","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two horned black-and-white rams. Anas said: And I sacrifice two rams."
"3930","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, who said: I heard Abd al-Aziz narrating from Anas, who said: The people of Madinah were struck by drought in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The people stood up to him on a Friday while he was on the pulpit delivering the sermon, and said: O Messenger of Allah, prices have risen and rain has been withheld, so supplicate to Allah to give us water. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hands and prayed for rain. He said: So we were rained upon, and it kept raining until the next Friday. He said: The people stood up to him while he was on the pulpit, and said: O Messenger of Allah, caravans have been cut off and buildings have collapsed, so supplicate to Allah to remove it from us. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled, then raised his hands and said: O Allah, around us and not upon us. He said: So it dispersed, and Madinah became like a crown while rain fell around it."
"3931","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wears it in this world will never wear it in the Hereafter, meaning silk."
"3932","Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn Umarah narrated to us, who said: I heard Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered the lavatory, would say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from male and female devils."
"3933","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit and Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the dawn prayer in darkness when he came from Khaybar, then mounted, and said: Allah is Most Great, Khaybar is ruined; when we descend in the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those who were warned. He said: So they came out hurrying in the streets, saying: Muhammad and the army. Hammad said: meaning the army. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prevailed, killed their fighters and took their offspring captive. He said: And Safiyyah belonged to Dihyah al-Kalbi, then afterwards she came to belong to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he married her and made her freedom her dowry. Abd al-Aziz said to Thabit: O Abu Muhammad, did you ask Anas what he gave her as dowry? And he said to you: He gave her herself as dowry? So Thabit smiled."
"3934","Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would shorten the prayer and complete it."
"3935","Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade men from using saffron perfume."
"3936","Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eat sahur, for there is blessing in sahur."
"3937","Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring of silver and engraved on it: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah, and said to the people: I have taken a ring, and its engraving is Muhammad, so let no one engrave upon its engraving."
"3938","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Mubarak, the freedman of Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took Mu'adh ibn Jabal as a rider behind him, and said: O Mu'adh, in the loudest voice. He said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. Then he called him a second time, then called him a third time in the loudest voice, and he said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. So he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not associate anything with Allah, Paradise is his."
"3939","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Mubarak narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Children of Israel split into seventy-one sects, and my nation will split into seventy-two sects, all of them in the Fire except the great multitude."
"3940","Muhammad narrated to us, Mubarak narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a funeral bier and said: Glad tidings for him, if he was not an arif (a petty official)."
"3941","Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he entered the lavatory, would say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from male and female devils."
"3942","Ishaq narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Mu'adh. He said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. Then he said: O Mu'adh. He said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah, three times, each time saying: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Give glad tidings to the people that whoever says: There is no god but Allah, will enter Paradise."
"3943","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Mubarak narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz, from Anas, I think it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Some people will come to my Pond and be snatched away from me, so I will say: O Lord, my companions. And it will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you."
"3944","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have had a ring made, so let no one engrave upon its engraving."
"3945","Muhammad ibn Bahr narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Suhaym ibn Abd Allah al-Shaybani narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Children of Israel split into seventy-one sects, and my nation will split into seventy-two sects, all of them in the Fire except the great multitude. Muhammad ibn Bahr said: meaning the congregation."
"3946","Muhammad ibn Bahr narrated to us, Mubarak narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be in this ummah swallowing up by the earth, and transformation, and quaking, and pelting."
"3947","Muhammad ibn Bahr narrated to us, Mubarak narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his Companions: Do not return after me as disbelievers, some of you striking the necks of others."
"3948","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Prophethood and messengership have come to an end, and the people were distressed. He said: There remain glad tidings, and they are a part of prophethood."
"3949","Dawud ibn Amr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, who said: I heard Mukhtar ibn Fulful - and he was the most tender-hearted narrator to narrate, his eyes shedding tears - mention, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: A man said to the Messenger of Allah: O best of creation! So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is Ibrahim (peace be upon him)."
"3950","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir and Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar, from Anas, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O best of creation. He said: That is Ibrahim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"3951","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas, who said: A man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O best of creation. He said: That is Ibrahim (peace be upon him)."
"3952","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was one day among us, he dozed off briefly, then raised his head smiling. So I said: What makes you laugh, O Messenger of Allah? He said: A surah has just been revealed to me. Then he recited: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Kind: Indeed, We have granted you al-Kawthar. So pray to your Lord and sacrifice. Indeed, your enemy is the one cut off. Then he said: Do you know what al-Kawthar is? We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: It is a river which my Lord has promised me, with much good in it; it is a basin to which my ummah will come on the Day of Resurrection, its vessels as numerous as the stars of the sky. A servant among them will be snatched away from it, and I will say: My Lord, he is from my ummah. Then He will say: You do not know what they innovated after you."
"3953","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer one day, and when he finished the prayer he turned to us with his face and said: O people, I am your imam, so do not precede me in bowing, nor in prostration, nor in standing, for I see you from in front of me and from behind me. Then he said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if you saw what I have seen, you would laugh little and weep much. They said: What have you seen, O Messenger of Allah? He said: I have seen Paradise and Hellfire."
"3954","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Al-Kawthar is a river in Paradise which my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, has promised me."
"3955","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, who said: I heard Mukhtar ibn Fulful say: I asked Anas about drinking from vessels, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade pitched vessels, and said: Every intoxicant is unlawful."
"3956","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar, judge of Aleppo, narrated to us, Mukhtar ibn Fulful narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the obligatory prayer on the ground sitting, and he sat in the glorification on the ground and gestured with gestures."
"3957","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban al-Kufi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, who said: I asked Anas ibn Malik about prayer after Asr, and he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab used to strike for praying after Asr. He said: We used to pray in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two rakahs after sunset before the Maghrib prayer. So I said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray them? He said: He used to see us praying them and he neither commanded us nor forbade us."
"3958","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Mukhtar ibn Fulful narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day, and turned from the prayer: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if you saw what I have seen, you would laugh little and weep much. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what have you seen? He said: I have seen Paradise and Hellfire."
"3959","Abu Bahz al-Saqr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn bint Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and entered a garden, then someone came and knocked on the door. He said: O Anas, stand and open for him, and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and give him glad tidings of the caliphate after me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I inform him? He said: Inform him. And behold, it was Abu Bakr. I said: Rejoice in Paradise, and rejoice in the caliphate after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then someone came and knocked on the door. He said: O Anas, stand and open for him, and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and give him glad tidings of the caliphate after Abu Bakr. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I inform him? He said: Inform him. He said: So I went out, and behold, it was Umar. He said: I said to him: Rejoice in Paradise, and rejoice in the caliphate after Abu Bakr. He said: Then someone came and knocked on the door. He said: O Anas, stand and open for him, and give him glad tidings of Paradise, and give him glad tidings of the caliphate after Umar, and that he will be killed. He said: So I went out, and behold, it was Uthman. He said: I said to him: Rejoice in Paradise, and in the caliphate after Umar, and that you will be killed. He said: So he entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, for what? By Allah, I have never sung, nor wished, nor touched my private part since I pledged allegiance to you. He said: That is it, O Uthman."
"3960","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the first to intercede in Paradise, and I am the one with the most followers among the prophets."
"3961","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am your imam, so do not hasten ahead of me in bowing nor in prostration, for I see you from in front of me and from behind me."
"3962","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will keep asking: What is such-and-such, what is such-and-such? Until they say: Allah created the creation, so who created Allah?"
"3963","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the like of it."
"3964","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day, and turned from the prayer, then came toward us and said: O people, I am your imam, so do not precede me in bowing, nor in prostration, nor in standing, nor in sitting, nor in leaving, for I see you from in front of me and from behind me. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if you saw what I have seen, you would laugh little and weep much. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what have you seen? He said: I have seen Paradise and Hellfire."
"3965","Uthman and Abu Bakr, sons of Abu Shaybah, narrated to us, both saying: Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the first to knock on the gate of Paradise."
"3966","Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am your imam, so do not hasten ahead of me in bowing nor in prostration, for I see you from in front of me and from behind me."
"3967","Uthman narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, who said: I asked Anas ibn Malik about drinks, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade pitched vessels, and said: Every intoxicant is unlawful. He said: I said to him: You have spoken the truth; drunkenness is unlawful. I only drink one or two drinks after food. He said: So he said to me: Whatever intoxicates in large amount, its small amount is unlawful. He said: Then wine was forbidden, and it is from grapes and dates, and honey and wheat, and barley and corn, and whatever ferments of that is wine."
"3968","Uthman narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the first of people to intercede in Paradise, and I am the one with the most followers among the prophets."
"3969","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, who said: Anas said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the first intercessor in Paradise."
"3970","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah said: Your ummah will keep asking: What is such-and-such? What is such-and-such? Until they say: This is Allah, Who created everything, so who created Allah?"
"3971","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No prophet among the prophets was believed as I was believed, and among the prophets there is a prophet whom none of his ummah believed except one man."
"3972","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Saminah al-Basri narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a drink in Yemen called bit and mizr, and he said: Whatever intoxicates is unlawful."
"3973","Sulayman ibn Nuh narrated to us, Husayn al-Jufi narrated to us, from Zaidah, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No prophet was believed as I was believed; among the prophets is one who will come on the Day of Resurrection with none of his ummah with him except one man."
"3974","Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the first of people to intercede in Paradise, and I am the one with the most followers among people."
"3975","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Saminah al-Basri narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shuayb ibn Shabur narrated to us, Said ibn Khalid narrated to us, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Guarding for a day in the path of Allah is better than one of you standing among his family for a thousand years, fasting its days and standing its nights; the year is three hundred and sixty days, and the day is a thousand years."
"3976","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Ali ibn Qadim narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ubayd al-Muktib, from al-Shabi, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed one day, or smiled, and said to his Companions: Will you not ask me what I laughed at? They said: O Messenger of Allah, what did you laugh at? He said: I marvel at the servant disputing with his Lord on the Day of Resurrection. He says: My Lord, did You not promise me that You would not wrong me? He says: Yes. He says: Then I do not accept any witness against me except from myself. Then He says: Is it not sufficient as a witness, along with the noble recording angels? He said: He repeats the speech several times. He said: Then his mouth is sealed, and his limbs speak of what he used to do. He said: Then he says: Away with you and perdition to you; it was for your sake that I was disputing."
"3977","Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl al-Tini, from Amir, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The first thing the servant will be held accountable for on the Day of Resurrection is the prayer. If it is complete, the rest of his deeds are complete; and if it is deficient, it will be said: Look, does he have voluntary prayers? If he has voluntary prayers, He says: Complete with it what is deficient of his prayer."
"3978","Abu Bakr ibn al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu al-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Ubaydullah al-Ashjai narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Said al-Thawri, from Ubayd al-Muktib, from Fudayl, from al-Shabi, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he laughed. He said: Do you know what I am laughing at? He said: We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: At the servant addressing his Lord. He says: My Lord, did You not protect me from injustice? He says: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: Yes. He says: Then I do not permit against myself except a witness from me. He says: Then He says: Your own self suffices as a witness against you, along with the noble recording angels as witnesses. He says: Then his mouth is sealed, and it is said to his limbs: Speak. He says: So they speak of his deeds. Then he says: He is left free to speak, and he says: Away with you and perdition to you; it was for your sake that I was contending."
"3979","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pass for six months by the door of Fatimah, daughter of the Prophet, at the dawn prayer, saying: Prayer, O people of the House, three times: Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O people of the House, and to purify you thoroughly."
"3980","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Shadhan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pass by the house of Fatimah for six months, and he mentioned the like of it."
"3981","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik, that the king of Rome gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a long shirt of sundus silk. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore it, and it is as if I am looking at its sleeves shaking. His Companions said: O Messenger of Allah, was this sent down to you from heaven? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, a handkerchief of the handkerchiefs of Sad ibn Muadh in Paradise is better than this. Then he sent it to Jafar, and Jafar wore it. He said: I did not send it to you to wear it. He said: What shall I do with it? He said: Send it to your brother, the Negus."
"3982","Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When al-Husayn was killed, his head was brought to Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad, and he began tapping with his cane on his front teeth, saying: He had handsome front teeth. So I said: By Allah, I will surely distress you. I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissing the spot of your cane on his mouth."
"3983","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ghundar narrated to us, from Shubah, from Ali ibn Zayd, who said: Anas said: A young slave girl among the slave girls of the Muslims would come and take the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would not pull his hand from her hand until she took him wherever she wished."
"3984","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: The voice of Abu Talhah in the army is better than a group. And when he met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he would kneel before him and say: My soul is a ransom for your soul, and my face a shield for your face."
"3985","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Ali ibn Zayd said: We were informed, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I attended the wedding feast of two of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they did not feed us bread or meat. He said: I said: Then what? He said: Hays."
"3986","Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us, Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you will be admitted to Paradise by his deeds. He said: We said: Not even you? He said: Not even me, unless my Lord covers me with mercy from Him and bounty."
"3987","Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of this hadith."
"3988","Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Dawud narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the people of Paradise? We said: Yes. He said: Every weak one, deemed weak, with two worn garments, to whom no attention is paid; if he swore by Allah, He would fulfill it. Among them is al-Bara ibn Malik."
"3989","Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The likeness of the five prayers is like a sweet flowing river, or a deep one, at the door of one of you; he bathes from it every day five times. What would remain of his dirt?"
"3990","Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, that he heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the first to take hold of the ring of the gate of Paradise and rattle it. Anas said: It is as if I am looking at him moving it with his hand."
"3991","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd and Thabit, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Uhud, when they pressed upon him, while he was among seven of the Ansar and two men of others: Who will repel them from us, and he will be my companion in Paradise? So a man of the Ansar stood and fought until he was killed. Then he said the like of that, and another man stood and fought until he was killed. He kept saying that until the seven were killed. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have not done justice to our companions."
"3992","Dawud ibn Amr narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Judan, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The voice of Abu Talhah in the army is better than a group."
"3993","Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I came upon men on the night I was taken by night, whose lips are cut with scissors of fire. I said: Who are these, O Jibril? He said: These are the preachers of your ummah; they command people to righteousness and forget themselves, while they recite the Book. Will they not understand?"
"3994","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, who said: Abu Talhah, when he was in an army, would scatter his quiver before him and say: My soul is a ransom for your soul, and my face a shield for your face. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The voice of Abu Talhah in the army is better than a group."
"3995","Jafar ibn Mihran narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, who said: When news of the killing of the people of Bir Maunah reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he stood in the dawn prayer, in the last rakah after bowing, and said: O Allah, curse Ril, and Dhakwan, and Usayyah, who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger. He said it three times, then said the takbir, then prostrated. I memorized that from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he did it for thirty days."
"3996","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Shadhan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit and Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the polytheists pressed upon him on the day of Uhud, said: Who will repel them from us, and he will be my companion in Paradise? So a man of the Ansar stood and fought until he was killed. Then another stood repelling them until seven were killed. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have not done justice to our companions."
"3997","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I passed on the night I was taken by night upon people whose lips are cut with scissors of fire. I said: Who are these? He said: These are preachers of the people of this world, among those who used to command people to righteousness and forget themselves, while they recite the Book. Will they not understand?"
"3998","Harun ibn Maruf narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Judan, from Anas: It is as if I am looking at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he says: I take hold of the ring of the gate and rattle it. And Sufyan said: Meaning with his hand."
"3999","Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, that Musab ibn al-Zubayr intended to kill the chief of the Ansar. Anas ibn Malik entered upon him and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Treat the Ansar well with good and kindness; accept from their doers of good, and overlook their doers of evil. He said: So Musab came down from his bed to his carpet, and stuck his skin, or his cheek, to it, or he said: he rolled about, and said: The command of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is upon the head and the eyes; the command of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is upon the head and the eyes. So he left him."
"4000","al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Rabi al-Jurjani narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The sky rained hail, and Abu Talhah said to us, while we were boys: Hand me, O Anas, some of that hail. He began eating it while fasting. I said: Are you not fasting? He said: Yes; this is neither food nor drink; it is only a blessing from heaven with which we purify our stomachs. Anas said: So I brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and he said: Take from your uncle."
"4001","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Said narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when news of the slain of Bir Maunah reached him, stood in the dawn prayer. He said: When he raised his head from the last rakah, he would stand upright, then say: O Allah, curse Ril, and Dhakwan, and Usayyah, who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger, three times. Then he would say the takbir and prostrate. He said: I memorized that from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he did it for thirty days."
"4002","Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Said ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman al-Kufi, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me, let him take his seat in Hellfire."
"4003","Abd al-Rahman ibn Sallam al-Jumahi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is mentioned in whose presence I am, let him send blessings upon me; for whoever sends blessings upon me once, Allah sends blessings upon him tenfold."
"4004","Husayn ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Minhal ibn Amr, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had supplications he never left; he used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from worry and grief, and inability and laziness, and miserliness and cowardice, and the burden of debt and the domination of men."
"4005","Ahmad ibn Hatim narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, who said: A man called Bayan narrated to me, who said: I said to Anas: Tell me of the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for prayer. He said: He used to pray Zuhr at the sun's decline, and pray Asr between your first prayer and Asr, and pray Maghrib at sunset, and pray Isha at the setting of the twilight, and pray the morning prayer at dawn when sight begins to open. All between that is time, or he said: prayer."
"4006","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, from Zuhayr, from Bayan, who said: I heard Anas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married a woman, and he sent me, so I invited men to the meal."
"4007","al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Hellfire will be presented on the Day of Resurrection in rows, and the believers will pass by them. A man of the people of Hellfire will see a man of the believers whom he knew in this world, and say: O so-and-so, do you not remember the day you sought my help for such-and-such a need? He said: That believer will remember that and recognize him, and will intercede for him to his Lord, and He will accept his intercession for him."
"4008","Nasr ibn Ali ibn Nasr narrated to us, Aththam ibn Ali narrated to us, from al-Amash, who said: Anas ibn Malik and al-Bara ibn Azib said: We would not bend our backs until we looked at the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating."
"4009","Zuhayr ibn Harb and Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a coat of armor pawned with a Jew, and he did not find what to redeem it with until he died."
"4010","Jubarah ibn Mughallis and Abd al-Ghaffar both narrated to us, both saying: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to the slave on account of the master, and woe to the master on account of the slave; and woe to the rich on account of the poor, and woe to the poor on account of the rich; and woe to the strong on account of the weak, and woe to the weak on account of the strong."
"4011","Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Sulayman al-Amash narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon a man visiting him, and behold, he had become like a chick from the severity of illness. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you not supplicate? Did you not ask? He said: Yes; I used to say: O Allah, whatever You will punish me with in the Hereafter, hasten it for me in this world. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then you cannot bear that. Why did you not say: My Lord, give me good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and shield us from the punishment of the Fire? So he said it, and he was cured."
"4012","Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Sulayman al-Amash said: I heard him mention, from Anas, raised up, that he said: When a man marries in addition to a wife, if she is a virgin, he stays with her seven days; and if she is previously married, he stays with her three days, then divides after that."
"4013","Abu Hisham al-Rifai narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Anas, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw the wind, he became frightened and said: O Allah, I ask You of the good of what it was commanded with. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what it was sent with."
"4014","al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man moving pebbles while in prayer. When he finished, he said to the man: That is your share of your prayer."
"4015","And from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled in Ramadan, fasting and breaking fast; his Companions fasted and broke fast, and neither criticized the other."
"4016","Wasil ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be invited to barley bread and rancid melted fat, and he would accept. And he had a coat of armor pawned with a Jew; he did not find what to redeem it with until he died."
"4017","al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, from al-Amash, from a man, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon a man visiting him and said: Do you desire anything? Do you desire kaka? He said: Yes. So they sought it for him."
"4018","Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yala al-Aslami narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Anas, who said: A boy of ours was martyred on the day of Uhud, and a rock was found tied to his stomach from hunger. His mother wiped the dust from his face and said: Glad tidings to you, my son, of Paradise. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What makes you know? Perhaps he used to speak of what did not concern him, and withhold what would not harm him."
"4019","Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, from Sharik, meaning from al-Amash, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever builds for Allah a mosque, even like the nesting place of a sandgrouse, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."
"4020","Ali ibn Jafar al-Ahmar Abu al-Hasan al-Kufi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The believer is not decreed any decree except that it is good for him."
"4021","Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to clean his teeth with the leftover of his ablution water."
"4022","Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, al-Amash informed us, who said: I was informed, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out one night intending to inform us of the Night of Decree, and we had been informed of it, but he heard noise in the mosque, so it was taken away from him."
"4023","Ibrahim narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, that Anas ibn Malik recited this verse: Indeed, the rising by night is very hard and most potent and good in recitation. A man said to him: We only recite it as: and most upright in speech. He said: Aqawm, aswab, ahya, and the likes of this are one."
"4024","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdah narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood between Quraysh and the Ansar in my house in Madinah."
"4025","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Asim, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood between Quraysh and the Ansar in my house in Madinah."
"4026","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Asim, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in Hellfire."
"4027","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, the wording being Zuhayr's, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Asim, from Anas, who said: I asked him about qunut, before bowing or after bowing? He said: Before bowing. He said: I said: People claim that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut after bowing. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only performed qunut for a month, supplicating against people who killed some of his Companions called the reciters."
"4028","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from Asim, who said: I asked Anas ibn Malik: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declare Madinah sacred? He said: Yes; it is sacred; Allah and His Messenger declared it sacred. Its grass is not to be cut. Whoever does that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."
"4029","Abd al-Ala narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) established brotherhood between the Muhajirun and the Ansar in the house of Anas in Madinah."
"4030","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O possessor of two ears."
"4031","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Ajlah narrated to us, from Asim, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in a single garment, crossing its two ends."
"4032","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, who said: I asked Anas ibn Malik about qunut. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month after bowing. He had one day sent seventy men to a people of the polytheists; and there was a people of the polytheists between whom and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) there was a covenant, yet the polytheists with whom there was a covenant between them and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) killed them. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month supplicating against them."
"4033","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Bukayr al-Jazari, from Sahl Abu al-Aswad, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: We were in a house, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at the door of the house and said: The leaders are from Quraysh, and I have a right over you, and they have a like of it over you, as long as they do three things: when they are asked for mercy, they show mercy; when they judge, they are just; and when they covenant, they fulfill. Whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."
"4034","Abu Bakr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, Sahl Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, from Bukayr al-Jazari, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah came to us while we were in the house of a man of the Ansar, and he took hold of the two doorposts, then said: The leaders are from Quraysh, and I have a right over you, and they have the like of that, as long as when they judge, they are just; when they are asked for mercy, they show mercy; and when they covenant, they fulfill. Whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people."
"4035","Husayn ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Umar ibn Hamzah narrated to us, Nafi, meaning Ibn Malik, narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no god but Allah shields the servant from the wrath of Allah, as long as they do not prefer the bargain of their world over their religion. When they do that, then he says: There is no god but Allah, Allah says: You have lied."
"4036","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Ziyad narrated to us, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seeking knowledge is obligatory upon every Muslim."
"4037","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Ibn Idris narrated to us, from Malik ibn Mighwal, from al-Zubayr ibn Adi, from Anas, who said: There is no day but the one after it is worse than it. We heard that from your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4038","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Zubayr ibn Adi, who said: We complained to Anas of what we meet at the hands of al-Hajjaj. He said: Be patient, for there will not come upon you a year, or a day, but the one after it is worse than it, until you meet your Lord. I heard it from your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4039","al-Azraq ibn Ali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Husayn al-Isbahani narrated to us, from al-Zubayr ibn Adi, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah said: None of you should outbid his brother, nor propose over the proposal of his brother."
"4040","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sleeping before Isha, and conversing after it."
"4041","Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Rijal narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, Thabit al-Araj said to me: Anas ibn Malik informed me, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: This ummah will remain in good as long as when it speaks, it speaks truthfully; when it judges, it is just; and when it is asked for mercy, it shows mercy."
"4042","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Sahba narrated to us, Abu Ghalib narrated to us, who said: I heard al-Ala ibn Ziyad say: I said to Anas: How will people be raised on the Day of Resurrection? He said: They will be raised while the sky showers upon them."
"4043","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Suddi, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to leave to his right."
"4044","Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Suddi, who said: I heard Anas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left the prayer to his right."
"4045","Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah and Humayd ibn Hilal, from Anas, who said: We were riding behind Abu Talhah, and his knee was touching the knee of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they both were crying out together with Hajj and Umrah."
"4046","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-Suddi, from Yahya ibn Abbad, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about wine being turned into vinegar. He said: No."
"4047","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Harb narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, Amr ibn Zaynab narrated to me, that Anas ibn Malik narrated to him, that Muadh said: O Messenger of Allah, what if there are rulers over us who do not follow your sunnah nor take your command; what do you command me concerning them? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no obedience to one who does not obey Allah."
"4048","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Hasan ibn Salih, from Khalid ibn al-Fazr, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, muzzat is unlawful: a mixture of unripe dates and ripe dates."
"4049","Zuhayr narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Hasan ibn Salih narrated to us, from Khalid ibn al-Fazr, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, muzzat is unlawful: a mixture of unripe dates and ripe dates."
"4050","Sufyan ibn Waki ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from my grandfather, from Qays ibn Wahb al-Hamdani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The boldest of people in questioning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were the bedouins. A bedouin came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, when is the Hour? He did not answer him until he came to the mosque and prayed, shortening the prayer. Then he turned to the bedouin and said: Where is the one asking about the Hour? And Sad passed by, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If this one lives until his life is consumed, there will not remain among you an eye that blinks."
"4051","Sufyan ibn Waki narrated to us, my father informed me, from my grandfather, from Qays ibn Wahb al-Hamdani, from Anas: The Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A hundred years from the Hijrah will not come while among you an eye blinks."
"4052","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Abu Hubayrah, from Anas ibn Malik, that Abu Talhah asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about orphans who inherited wine. He said: Pour it out. He said: Shall I not make it vinegar? He said: No."
"4053","al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated to us, Mushir ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Sila - trustworthy - narrated to us, Isa ibn Umar narrated to us, from Ismail al-Suddi, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a bird with him, and he said: O Allah, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to eat with me of this bird. Abu Bakr came, and he turned him away. Then Umar came, and he turned him away. Then Ali came, and he gave him permission."
"4054","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, and Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, who said: I asked Anas ibn Malik, saying: Inform me of something you remember from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Where did he pray Zuhr on the day of Tarwiyah? He said: In Mina. I said: Where did he pray Asr on the day of departure? He said: At al-Abtah. Then he said: Do as your rulers do."
"4055","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Qays narrated to us, who said: I heard Amr, freedman of al-Muttalib, say: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: Among the supplication of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he returned from Khaybar was: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from worry and grief, and inability and laziness, and cowardice and miserliness, and the burden of debt and the domination of men."
"4056","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Bishr, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before the emergence of the Dajjal there will be more than seventy dajjals."
"4057","Abu al-Ashath al-Ijli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humran narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: We went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a funeral, and he saw women. He said: Do you carry him? He said: Will you bury him? They said: No. He said: Then return, bearing sin and without reward."
"4058","Amr ibn Husayn narrated to us, al-Mutamir narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to me, from Jabir ibn Yazid, from Abu Nasr, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me a kunyah with a herb I had gathered, meaning Hamzah."
"4059","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Bishr, from Anas ibn Malik, raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning His saying: By your Lord, We will surely question them all, about what they used to do. He said, about: There is no god but Allah."
"4060","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from inability and laziness, and decrepitude, and cowardice and miserliness, and the punishment of the grave, and the evil of the False Messiah, the Dajjal."
"4061","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Muadh ibn Muadh and Jarir narrated to us, both saying: Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, Anas narrated to us, who said: Two men sneezed before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he responded to one of them with tashmit and left the other. He said: This one praised Allah, and this one did not praise Allah."
"4062","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in Hellfire."
"4063","Zahmawayh narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"4064","Zuhayr narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will look into what Abu Jahl has done? He said: So Abdullah ibn Masud went and found him struck by the two sons of Afra until he was cold. He said: O enemy of Allah, are you Abu Jahl? He said: Is there above a man killed by his people, or killed by you?"
"4065","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: There was a man called Anjashah driving the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Anjashah, gently, your driving with the glass vessels."
"4066","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mixing unripe dates and ripe dates."
"4067","Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas, who said: It was mentioned to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among you are a people who worship until they impress people and their own selves impress them; they pass out of the religion as the arrow passes out of the game."
"4068","Wahb narrated to us, Khalid informed us, from al-Taymi, from Anas: One of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed me that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on the night he was taken by night, passed by Musa while he was praying in his grave."
"4069","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, who said: Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Zuray, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only gouged out their eyes because they gouged out the eyes of the herdsmen."
"4070","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, from his father, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: On the night I was taken by night, I saw people whose tongues are cut with scissors of fire, or he said: of iron. I said: Who are these, O Jibril? He said: Preachers of your ummah."
"4071","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Taymi narrated to us, who said: I heard Anas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me, let him take his seat in Hellfire."
"4072","Ismail ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid al-Qurashi al-Raqqi narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Ali ibn Fudayl al-Malti narrated to us, who said: I heard Sulayman al-Taymi say: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: I performed ablution for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a month before his death, and he wiped over the two socks and the turban."
"4073","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, Sahl ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Taymi, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the call to prayer is made, the gates of heaven are opened and supplication is answered."
"4074","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, who said: Two men sneezed before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he responded to one of them with tashmit - or he said: with tasmit - and left the other. It was said: They are two men who sneezed; you responded to one and left the other? He said: This one praised Allah, and this one did not praise Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"4075","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Badr: Who will look into what Abu Jahl has done? Ibn Masud went and found him struck by the two sons of Afra until he was cold. He said: Are you Abu Jahl? He said: Is there above a man you have killed? Sulayman said: Or killed by his people."
"4076","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, who said: Umm Sulaym was with the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon them while a driver was driving them. He said: O Anjashah, gently, your driving with the glass vessels."
"4077","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, al-Taymi narrated to us, who said: I heard Anas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me, let him take his seat in Hellfire. And he said: He narrated it to us thus twice, then he narrated it to us another time, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in Hellfire."
"4078","Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade combining unripe dates and fresh ripe dates."
"4079","Shabab Khalifah ibn Khayyat al-Usfuri narrated to us, al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, who said: I heard my father, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: A man used to assign to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) charities from his palm trees, until Qurayzah and al-Nadir were conquered, and the Messenger of Allah began returning after that. My family ordered me to come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him for what they had given him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had given them to Umm Ayman. So I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he gave them to me. Umm Ayman came and twisted the garment around my neck, saying: No, by the One besides Whom there is no god, he shall not give them to you, when he has given them to me. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was saying: For you is such-and-such, and for you is such-and-such - I think he said: while she was saying: No, by Allah - until he gave her ten times their like."
"4080","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from his father, from Anas, that a man used to assign to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) palm trees from his land, until Qurayzah and al-Nadir were conquered over him, and after that he began returning what he had been given. Anas said: My family ordered me to come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him for what he had been given, or part of it. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had given it to Umm Ayman. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he gave them to me. Umm Ayman came and placed the garment on my neck, saying: By Allah, he shall not give them to you, when he has given them to me. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Umm Ayman, leave him, and for you is such-and-such. She says: No, by the One besides Whom there is no god. He kept saying: Such-and-such, until he gave her ten times their like, or close to ten times their like."
"4081","Suwayd ibn Said narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I saw Paradise and Hellfire in this wall; I have never seen like today in good and evil."
"4082","Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, who said: I heard my father, that a man narrated to him, from Anas ibn Malik, that he said: One of us would straighten his backbone in prayer behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) settled into prostration - or he said: onto the ground - then he would prostrate at that."
"4083","Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, who said: I heard my father narrate, from Anas, who said: It was said: O Prophet of Allah, if only you would come to Abdullah ibn Ubayy? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out riding a donkey, and the Muslims set out walking, and it was salty land. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him, he said: Keep away from me; by Allah, the stench of your donkey has harmed me. A man of the Ansar said: By Allah, the donkey of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is sweeter in smell than you. A man of his people became angry for Abdullah, and the companions of each of them became angry. There was beating among them with palm stalks, hands, and sandals. We were informed that it was revealed concerning them: And if two parties of the believers fight, make peace between them."
"4084","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated to us, Mutamir narrated to us, from his father, who said: I heard Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on the night he was taken by night, passed by Musa while he was praying in his grave. Anas said: He mentioned that he was carried upon al-Buraq, and he tied the animal - or he said: the horse. Abu Bakr said: Describe it to me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said ... and mentioned a word. He said: I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah. And Abu Bakr had seen it."
"4085","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Sulayman al-Taymi, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I passed by Musa while he was praying in his grave."
"4086","Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever performs ablution, then with it - and how excellent - and whoever bathes, bathing is better - meaning: on Friday."
"4087","Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Hiql ibn Ziyad, and from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: From Asr until sunset is more beloved to me than freeing eight of the children of Ismail, all of them Muslim - meaning: that I remember Allah."
"4088","Khalaf ibn Hisham narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Maymun, al-Raqashi narrated to us, who said: Anas, when he narrated this hadith to us, would say to us: By Allah, it is not what you and your companions do - meaning: one of you sits and you gather around him and he preaches. Rather, when they prayed the morning prayer, they would sit in circles, reciting the Quran and learning the obligations and the sunnahs."
"4089","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril came to me with a white mirror in which was a black spot. I said: What is this? He said: This is Friday, and in it is an hour."
"4090","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Children are the servants of the people of Paradise."
"4091","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, Yazid al-Raqashi narrated to us, from Anas, who said: We were sitting with the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - perhaps sixty men - and he would narrate the hadith to us, then he would go in for his need, and we would review it among ourselves, one then another, then we would stand as though it had been sown in our hearts."
"4092","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Abdi narrated to us, Ma'bad ibn Khalid al-Ansari narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Among my brothers among the prophets who passed before, there were eight thousand prophets, then there was 'Isa son of Maryam, then I was."
"4093","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, al-Salt - meaning Ibn Hajjaj - narrated to us, and al-Hajjaj al-Khassaf narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever helps his brother with his need and is kind to him, it is binding upon Allah to provide him with servants from among the servants of Paradise."
"4094","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Sallam ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Zayd al-'Ammi, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The sea was split for the Children of Israel on the day of 'Ashura."
"4095","Al-Fadl ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Abu 'Ubaydah narrated to us, from Muhtasib, who said: Yazid al-Raqashi narrated to me, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who attends the funeral of a Muslim man except that he has a qirat of reward, and if he remains seated until it is leveled over him (i.e. burial is completed) he has two qirats of reward, each qirat like Uhud."
"4096","Al-Fadl ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, Abu 'Ubaydah narrated to us, from Muhtasib, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas, who said: Abu Musa sat in his house and people gathered to him, and he began reciting the Qur'an to them. He said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah and said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not amaze you with Abu Musa - he sat in a house and people gathered to him and he began reciting the Qur'an to them? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Can you seat me where none of them can see me? He said: Yes. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out, and the man seated him where none of them could see him, and he heard the recitation of Abu Musa. He said: He said: He recites upon a flute from among the flutes of the family of Dawud."
"4097","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to have his lifespan extended and his provision increased, let him join his ties of kinship."
"4098","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, 'Umar ibn Yunus al-Hanafi narrated to us, 'Ikrimah narrated to us, Yazid al-Raqashi narrated to us, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There are three traits, whoever has them in him is a hypocrite, even if he fasts and prays and performs Hajj and 'Umrah, and says: I am a Muslim: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks his promise, and when he is entrusted he betrays."
"4099","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, 'Umar ibn Yunus narrated to us, 'Ikrimah narrated to us, Yazid al-Raqashi narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I said: O Abu Hamzah, there are people who testify against us with disbelief and polytheism. Anas said: They are the worst of creation and creatures. He said: And they deny the Hawd (Basin). He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I have a basin whose width is like what is between Aylah and the Ka'bah - or he said: San'a' - whiter than milk and sweeter than honey, in it are vessels as numerous as the stars of the sky, replenished by two spouts from Paradise; whoever denies it will not attain drink from it."
"4100","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, 'Umar ibn Yunus al-Hanafi narrated to us, 'Ikrimah narrated to us, who said: I heard Yazid al-Raqashi say: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Between the servant and disbelief and polytheism is the abandonment of prayer; when he abandons prayer he has disbelieved."
"4101","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz - meaning al-Majishun - narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I asked my Lord concerning the heedless little ones of human offspring that He not punish them, and He granted them to me."
"4102","Salih ibn Malik narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn al-Majishun narrated to us, with the same (hadith)."
"4103","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a stone like seven pregnant camels with their fat and their young were cast into Hell, it would fall for seventy years without reaching its bottom."
"4104","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Nili narrated to us, Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he heard him say: Charity and joining the ties of kinship - Allah increases lifespan thereby, and wards off by them an evil death, and Allah wards off thereby what is disliked and dreaded."
"4105","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Nili narrated to us, Salih narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah said: My intercession is for the people of major sins of my ummah."
"4106","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Nili narrated to us, Salih al-Murri narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah bestows His bounty upon the people of 'Arafat, boasting of them to the angels, saying: O My angels, look at My servants, disheveled and dusty, coming to Me striking forth from every deep mountain pass. I call you to witness that I have answered their supplication, granted their desire, given their wrongdoers to their righteous, and given their righteous all that they asked Me except for the claims between them. Then when the people pour forth to Jam' (Muzdalifah) and stand and return to desire and seeking from Allah, He says: O My angels, My servants stood and returned to desire and seeking; I call you to witness that I have answered their supplication, granted their desire, given their wrongdoers to their righteous, given their righteous all that they asked Me, and taken upon Myself the claims between them."
"4107","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Nili narrated to us, Salih narrated to us, from Thabit, and Ja'far ibn Zayd, and Yazid al-Raqashi, and Maymun ibn Siyah, from Anas, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever prays the morning prayer (al-ghadah) is under the protection of Allah, so beware lest Allah demand from you anything of His protection."
"4108","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Nili narrated to us, Salih narrated to us, from Thabit, and Yazid al-Raqashi, and Maymun ibn Siyah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, your Lord is Modest and Generous; He is shy that one of you should extend his hands to Him and He return them empty."
"4109","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Abu al-'Umays 'Utbah ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the mu'adhdhin calls the adhan, the gates of heaven are opened and supplication between the adhan and the iqamah is not rejected."
"4110","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us, Musa ibn 'Ubaydah narrated to us, Yazid al-Raqashi narrated to me, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no spot on which Allah is remembered with prayer or with remembrance except that it rejoices thereby to its limit among the seven earths, and boasts over the spots around it; and there is no servant who stands in a desert land intending prayer except that the earth adorns itself for him."
"4111","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, al-Rabi' ibn Subayh and Masruq Abu 'Abdullah al-Sami narrated to us, both saying: Yazid al-Raqashi narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting the three days of tashriq after the day of sacrifice."
"4112","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to pray over 'Abdullah ibn Ubayy, so Jibril took hold of his garment and said: {And never pray over any of them who dies, ever, nor stand over his grave}."
"4113","Abu Ma'mar Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Waqid ibn Salamah, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies on Friday is protected from the punishment of the grave."
"4114","Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Layth, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever seeks refuge with Allah ten times in a day from Satan, Allah assigns to him an angel to ward the devils away from him."
"4115","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Rawh ibn al-Musayyab narrated to us, Yazid al-Raqashi narrated to us, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My intercession is for the people of major sins of my ummah. He said: He said: The confirmation of this is in the Qur'an. He said: So he recited to us: {If you avoid the major sins of what you are forbidden, We will expiate from you your evil deeds and admit you to a noble entrance}. So these are those who avoid the major sins, and those are those who committed the major sins - remaining for them is the intercession of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So Yazid said to Anas: You spoke the truth."
"4116","Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Durust ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Yazid al-Raqashi narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The sun and the moon are two hamstrung oxen in the Fire."
"4117","Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Kahmas ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade fasting five days of the year: the day of Fitr, the day of sacrifice, and the days of tashriq."
"4118","Qatan ibn Nusayr al-Ghubari narrated to us, 'Ubayd ibn Maymun al-Raqashi narrated to us, Yazid al-Raqashi narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Is none of you able to recite {Say: He is Allah, One} three times in a night? For it equals a third of the Qur'an."
"4119","Muhammad ibn Bahr narrated to us, al-Mu'alla ibn Maymun al-Mujashi'i narrated to us, Yazid al-Raqashi narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is kind to a believer or helps him with any of his needs, whether small or great, it is binding upon Allah to provide him with servants from among the servants of Paradise."
"4120","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Sakhr, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays the morning prayer (al-ghadah) and then his protection is violated, the sanctuary of Allah has been violated and his protection betrayed, and I am the claimant for his protection."
"4121","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Hajjaj narrated to us, from al-Rabi' ibn Subayh, Yazid al-Raqashi narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The son of Adam will be brought on the Day of Resurrection as though he were a badhaj - and perhaps he said: as though he were a camel - and He will say: Son of Adam, I am the best partner; look at your deed which you did for Me and I will reward you, and look at your deed which you did for other than Me, so let him for whom you did it reward you."
"4122","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, Durust ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Yazid al-Raqashi narrated to me, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has died. He said: Was he not with us just now? They said: Yes. He said: Glory be to Allah, as though it were a seizure in anger; the deprived is he who is deprived of his bequest."
"4123","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Yazid al-Raqashi narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to have his lifespan extended and his provision increased, let him join his ties of kinship."
"4124","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Yazid al-Raqashi narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first thing Allah obligated upon people of their religion is prayer, and the last thing that remains is prayer, and the first thing they will be reckoned for is prayer. Allah says: Look into the prayer of My servant; if it was complete it is written complete, and if it is found deficient, He says: Look, does he have voluntary (prayer)? If voluntary is found for him, the obligatory is completed from the voluntary. Then He says: Look, is his zakah complete? If his zakah is found complete it is written complete, and if it was deficient, He says: Look, does he have charity? If he has charity, his zakah is completed for him from the charity."
"4125","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That I sit with people remembering Allah from the early morning until the sun rises is dearer to me than all upon which the sun has risen."
"4126","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, al-Mu'alla ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That I sit with people remembering Allah from the 'Asr prayer until the sun sets is dearer to me than freeing eight persons from the children of Isma'il."
"4127","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, 'Umar ibn Yunus narrated to us, 'Ikrimah narrated to us, Yazid al-Raqashi narrated to us - at the basin of Zamzam while people were gathered around him from Quraysh and others - who said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, who said: There was a man in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who would go out in expeditions with the Messenger of Allah, and when he returned and unpacked from his mount, he would head to the mosque of the Messenger and pray in it at length, until some of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to consider him superior to them. One day he passed while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting among his Companions, and one of his Companions said to him: O Prophet of Allah, this is that man; so either the Prophet of Allah sent for him or he came of his own accord. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him coming, he said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, between his eyes is a smear of Satan. When he stood over the gathering, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Did you say to yourself when you stood over the gathering: There is none among the people better than me? He said: Yes. Then he left and went to a side of the mosque, drew a line with his foot, then aligned his heels and stood praying. The Messenger of Allah said: Which of you will stand to this man and kill him? Abu Bakr stood, and the Messenger of Allah said: Did you kill the man? He said: I found him praying so I was awed. The Messenger of Allah said: Which of you will stand to this man and kill him? 'Umar said: I will, and he took the sword and found him standing praying, so he returned. The Messenger of Allah said to 'Umar: Did you kill the man? He said: O Prophet of Allah, I found him praying so I was awed. The Messenger of Allah said: Which of you will stand to this man and kill him? 'Ali said: I will. The Messenger of Allah said: You are for him if you reach him. 'Ali went and did not find him, so he returned. The Messenger of Allah said: Did you kill the man? He said: I did not know which path of the earth he took. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the first horn to come out of my ummah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had you killed him - or had he been killed - no two in my ummah would have differed. The Children of Israel split into seventy-one sects, and this ummah - meaning his ummah - will split into seventy-two sects, all of them in the Fire except one sect. We said: O Prophet of Allah, which sect is that? He said: The congregation (al-jama'ah). Yazid al-Raqashi said: So I said to Anas: O Abu Hamzah, and where is the congregation? He said: With your rulers, with your rulers."
"4128","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, 'Abbad ibn 'Abbad al-Muhallabi narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, what of one of us who speaks to himself of a thing such that falling from the sky and being severed is dearer to him than speaking of it? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is pure faith."
"4129","Hafs ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar al-Hulwani narrated to us, Durust ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas, who said: I was walking with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said to me: O my son, call for me for ablution water from this house. I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is asking for ablution water? He said: Tell him our bucket is the skin of a dead animal. He said: Ask them, did they tan it? They said: Yes. He said: Its tanning is its purification."
"4130","'Abd al-Ghaffar ibn 'Abdullah narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I knock at the gate of Paradise and a gate of gold is opened with its rings of silver, and the Greatest Light meets me, and I fall prostrate, and I am inspired with praise of Allah such as none before me was inspired with. It is said to me: Raise your head, ask and you will be given, speak and you will be heard, intercede and your intercession will be accepted. I say: My ummah. It is said: Yours is whoever had in his heart a barley-grain weight of faith. He said: Then I prostrate a second time, then I am inspired with the like of that, and the like of that is said to me, and I say: My ummah. It is said to me: Yours is whoever had in his heart a mustard-seed weight of faith. Then I prostrate a third time, and the like of that is said to me, then I raise my head and say: My ummah. It is said to me: Yours is whoever said: There is no god but Allah, sincerely."
"4131","Al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated to us, 'Aththam narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dreams have an inner meaning, so give them kunyas by their kunyas, and name them by their names; and the dream belongs to the first interpreter."
"4132","Ahmad ibn Ishaq Abu 'Abdullah al-Jawhari al-Basri narrated to us, Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Musa ibn 'Ubaydah al-Rabadhi narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah sent eight thousand prophets: four thousand to the Children of Israel, and four thousand to the rest of mankind."
"4133","Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Basri narrated to us, Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Musa ibn 'Ubaydah al-Rabadhi narrated to us, Yazid al-Raqashi informed me, Anas ibn Malik informed me, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: There is no servant but that he has two gates in heaven: a gate through which his deed enters, and a gate through which his deed and his speech go out. When he dies they miss him and weep over him. And he recited this verse: {Neither heaven nor earth wept over them}. He mentioned that they would not do a righteous deed on earth that would weep over them, nor would there ascend for them to heaven any good speech nor righteous deed of theirs that would miss them and weep over them."
"4134","'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from 'Imran ibn Zayd, Yazid al-Raqashi narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O people, weep; if you do not weep then pretend to weep, for the people of the Fire weep in the Fire until their tears flow over their faces as though they were streams, until the tears cease, then it flows - meaning blood - so that the eyes become sore; if ships were launched in it they would sail."
"4135","Al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Shihab ibn Khirash narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I fear for my ummah after me five things: denial of divine decree, and belief in the stars."
"4136","Abu Ibrahim al-Tarjuman Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, 'Ubayd ibn Maymun narrated to us, Yazid al-Raqashi narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is none of you able to recite in the night {Say: He is Allah, One}, for it equals the whole Qur'an. He said: And he said: People cannot do without a chief ('arif), and the chief is in the Fire. He said: And the policeman (al-shurti) will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and it will be said to him: Put down your whip and enter the Fire."
"4137","Muhammad ibn Ghalib wrote to me in his handwriting, who said: Al-Muthanna narrated to me - Abu Ya'la said: meaning my grandfather - Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I knock at the gate of Paradise, and a gate of gold is opened for me with its rings of silver, and the Greatest Light meets me, and I fall prostrate, and I am inspired with praise of Allah such as none before me was inspired with. It is said to me: Raise your head, ask and you will be given, intercede and your intercession will be accepted, speak and you will be heard. I say: My ummah. It is said: Yours is whoever had in his heart a barley-grain weight of faith. He said: Then I prostrate a second time and am inspired with the like of that, and I say: My ummah. It is said to me: Yours is whoever had in his heart a mustard-grain weight of faith. Then I prostrate a third time and am inspired with the like of that, and the like of that is said to me, then I raise my head and say: My ummah. It is said: Yours is whoever said: There is no god but Allah, sincerely."
"4138","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Sallam narrated to us, from Zayd al-'Ammi, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped to rest one night, and Bilal called the adhan. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says like his saying and witnesses like his witnessing, for him is Paradise."
"4139","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ar'arah narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Sadusi narrated to us, Maymun ibn 'Ajlan narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Siyah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There are no two Muslims who meet and one of them takes his companion by the hand except that it is binding upon Allah to answer their supplication, and He does not turn back their hands until He forgives them."
"4140","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ar'arah narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Maymun ibn 'Ajlan narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Siyah, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim servant who comes to a brother of his visiting him for the sake of Allah except that a caller from heaven calls to him: You are blessed, and Paradise is blessed for you; otherwise Allah says in the kingdom of His Throne: He visited for My sake, and his hospitality is upon Me, and I am not pleased for him with any hospitality less than Paradise."
"4141","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ar'arah narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Maymun ibn 'Ajlan narrated to us, from Maymun ibn Siyah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There are no people who gather remembering Allah, intending thereby only His Face, except that a caller from heaven calls to them: Rise forgiven, your evil deeds have been replaced with good deeds."
"4142","I heard Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ar'arah say: I heard Muslim ibn Ibrahim say: Sallam ibn Miskin narrated to us, who said: Maymun ibn Siyah is the master of the reciters."
"4143","Muhammad ibn al-Faraj Abu Ja'far narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, Musa ibn 'Ubaydah narrated to us, Hud ibn 'Ata informed me, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: In the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) there was a man whose worship and striving amazed us; we had described him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by name and he did not recognize him, and we described him by his description and he did not recognize him. While we were mentioning him, the man appeared. We said: This is he. He said: You are telling me of a man upon whose face is a smear of Satan. He came until he stood over them without greeting. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: I adjure you by Allah, did you say when you stood over the gathering: There is none among the people better - or more excellent - than me? He said: O Allah, yes. Then he entered to pray. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will kill the man? Abu Bakr said: I will. He entered upon him and found him praying, and said: Glory be to Allah, shall I kill a man who prays, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has forbidden striking those who pray? So he came out. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What did you do? He said: I disliked killing him while he prays, when you have forbidden striking those who pray. He said: Who will kill the man? 'Umar said: I will. He entered and found him placing his face (in prostration). 'Umar said: Abu Bakr is better than me, so he came out. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What? He said: I found him placing his face for Allah so I disliked killing him. He said: Who will kill the man? 'Ali said: I will. He said: You, if you reach him. He said: He entered upon him and found him already gone, so he returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said to him: What? He said: I found him already gone. He said: Had he been killed, no two men of my ummah would have differed, its first and its last. Musa said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ka'b say: He is the one whom 'Ali killed: Dhu al-Thudayyah."
"4144","'Amr ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Musa ibn 'Ubaydah narrated to us, from Hud ibn 'Ata, from Anas, from Abu Bakr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade striking those who pray."
"4145","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Sa'id, who said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, who said: Abu Talhah sent me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to invite him, having prepared food for him. He said: I came while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with the people. He said: He looked at me and I was shy, so I said: Answer (the invitation of) Abu Talhah. He said to the people: Stand. Abu Talhah said: O Messenger of Allah, I prepared only a little for you. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped it and invoked blessing in it, and said: Admit a group of my companions, ten. He said: Eat. He brought forth something between his fingers, and they ate until they were full and went out. He said: Admit ten. They ate until they were full and went out. He kept admitting ten men and sending out ten until none of them remained except he entered and ate until full. He said: Then he prepared it, and it was as it was when they ate from it."
"4146","Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had two freedmen: a Habashi and a Nabati. They reviled one another while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was listening. One of them said to his companion: O Habashi! The other said: O Nabati! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not say this; you are only two men from among the Companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4147","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Zayd al-'Ammi, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Supplication between the adhan and the iqamah is not rejected."
"4148","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, who said: I said to Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah: Did you hear Anas say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The son of the sister of a people is from them? He said: Yes."
"4149","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Masruq, from Husayn ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Shaybani, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas, who said: I do not recognize anything of people's affairs except the qiblah."
"4150","Abu Hammam narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, Jald ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Let the menstruating woman wait five, seven, eight, nine, ten days; when ten have passed she is mustahadah (suffering non-menstrual bleeding)."
"4151","Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn 'Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Hudbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalalah narrated to us, Bakr and Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas: Abu Talhah saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hungry with his belly folded, so he came to Umm Sulaym and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hungry with his belly folded; do you have anything? She said: We have only about a mudd of barley flour. He said: Knead it and prepare it; perhaps we may invite the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to eat with us. He said: She kneaded it and baked it and it became a loaf. He said: He said to me: Invite the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while people were with him - Mubarak said: I think he said: some eighty-odd - He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Talhah invites you. He said to his Companions: Answer (the invitation of) Abu Talhah. I came hastening until I informed him that he had come with his Companions. Bakr said: He pinched me a pinch. Thabit said: Abu Talhah said: The Messenger of Allah knows what is in my house better than me. Both said together, from Anas: Abu Talhah met him and said: O Messenger of Allah, we have nothing but a loaf; I saw you hungry with folded belly so I ordered Umm Sulaym and she made a loaf for you. He said: He called for the loaf and called for the bowl and placed it in it, and said: Is there any ghee? Abu Talhah said: There was something in the skin. He said: He brought it. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Talhah began squeezing it until something came out, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped his forefinger, then wiped the loaf, and it swelled. He said: In the name of Allah. The loaf kept swelling until I saw the loaf in the bowl rising. He said: Invite ten of my Companions. I invited ten for him. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his hand in the middle of the loaf and said: Eat, in the name of Allah. They ate from around the loaf until they were full. He said: Then he said: Invite ten others for me. I invited ten others for him, and he said: Eat, in the name of Allah. They ate from around the loaf until they were full. He kept inviting ten by ten, eating from that loaf until they were full, while the middle of the loaf where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had placed his hand remained as it was."
"4152","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Ghalib al-Qattan, from Bakr, from Anas, who said: We would pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in intense heat, and when one of us could not place his face firmly on the ground he would spread his garment and prostrate on it."
"4153","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Khalid ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Bukayr al-Sulami, from Ghalib al-Qattan, from Bakr al-Muzani, from Anas, who said: When we prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we would prostrate on our garments for fear of the heat."
"4154","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Amir narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, from Bakr ibn 'Abdullah, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram for both together. He said: I mentioned that to Ibn 'Umar, and he said: He entered ihram for Hajj. I mentioned that to Anas, and he said: You count us only as children."
"4155","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Khalid, from Bakr ibn 'Abdullah, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Labbayk, with Hajj and 'Umrah."
"4156","Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, from Ghalib, from Bakr ibn 'Abdullah, from Anas, who said: We would pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in intense heat; one of us would take pebbles in his hand, and when they cooled he would place them and prostrate on them."
"4157","Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Ubaydullah al-Jubayri narrated to us, who said: I heard Bakr ibn 'Abdullah al-Muzani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The prohibition of wine came down, and I entered upon some of my companions while it was before them, so I struck it with my foot then said: Go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the prohibition of wine has come down. He said: Their drink that day was unripe dates and ripe dates."
"4158","Jubarah ibn Mughallis narrated to us, who said: Hafs ibn Subayh al-Shaybani narrated to me - Jubarah said: among the most devout of people - from Malik ibn Dinar, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man speaks then turns (glances aside), it is a trust."
"4159","Jubarah ibn Mughallis narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Malik ibn Dinar, from Anas, who said: I prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr, and 'Umar, and 'Uthman, and 'Ali, and they would begin the recitation with {All praise belongs to Allah, Lord of the worlds}, and they would recite {Master of the Day of Judgment}."
"4160","Muhammad ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwa'i narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, the son-in-law of Malik ibn Dinar, from Malik ibn Dinar, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I came to the lowest heaven on the night I was taken by night, and I saw therein men whose tongues and lips were being cut with scissors of fire. I said: O Jibril, who are these? He said: These are preachers from your ummah."
"4161","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, 'Ajlan ibn 'Abdullah of Banu 'Adi narrated to me, from Malik ibn Dinar, from Anas, who said: When death came to Abu Salamah, Umm Salamah said: To whom do you entrust me? He said: O Allah, You are better for Umm Salamah than Abu Salamah. When he died, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proposed to her. She said: I am advanced in age. He said: I am older than you in age; dependents are upon Allah and His Messenger; as for jealousy, I hope Allah will remove it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her, and sent to her two millstones and a jar for water."
"4162","Ghassan ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab and 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas ibn Malik: The Prophet freed Safiyyah and made her freedom her dowry."
"4163","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Safiyyah bint Huyayy and gave her freedom as her dowry."
"4164","Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah and made her freedom her dowry."
"4165","Ghassan narrated to us, from Hammad, from Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a basket containing unripe dates, and he said: {The parable of a good word is as a good tree, its root firm and its branches in the sky, yielding its fruit at all times by permission of its Lord}. He said: It is the palm tree. {And the parable of an evil word is as an evil tree, uprooted from above the earth, having no stability}. He said: It is the colocynth. Shu'ayb said: I informed Abu al-'Aliyah of that, and he said: Thus we used to hear."
"4166","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Ta'i Abu Malik narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most complete of people in faith are the best of them in character; good character attains the rank of fasting and prayer."
"4167","Abu Yusuf al-Jizi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yunus ibn 'Ubayd, from Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah and made her freedom her dowry."
"4168","Qatan ibn Nusayr al-Ghubari narrated to us, Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah and made her freedom her dowry."
"4169","'Umar ibn Shabbah narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Marwan ibn al-Hakam ibn Yazid ibn 'Umayr al-Usayyidi narrated to us, 'Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays over a funeral, a qirat is written for him; if he waits until its completion is decreed, two qirats are written for him."
"4170","Sa'id ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab narrated to me, Shu'ayb informed me, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to like pumpkin (al-qar')."
"4171","Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us, 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Shu'ayb, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have repeatedly enjoined upon you the siwak."
"4172","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, 'Ubayd ibn Sa'id al-Qurashi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make things easy and do not make them hard, give calm and do not drive away."
"4173","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, 'Ubayd ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Blessing is in the forelocks of horses."
"4174","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn 'Amir narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray in sheep pens before mosques were built."
"4175","'Abd al-Ghaffar ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Kurayd ibn Rawahah al-'Ayshi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Love of the Ansar is the sign of every believer and hypocrite; whoever loves the Ansar, it is out of love for me that he loves them, and whoever hates them, it is out of hatred for me that he hates them."
"4176","'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Shu'bah, Abu al-Tayyah narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hear and obey, even if a Habashi whose head is like a raisin is appointed over you."
"4177","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Blessing is in the forelocks of horses."
"4178","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas, who said: The site of the mosque of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) belonged to Banu al-Najjar, and in it were palm trees, tilled land, and graves from the graves of Jahiliyyah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Name a price for me. They said: We seek no price for it except with Allah. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the palms cut down, the tilled land spoiled, and the graves exhumed. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray before that in sheep pens and wherever prayer overtook him."
"4179","Ja'far ibn Mihran al-Sabbak narrated to us, 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the signs of the Hour are that knowledge is lifted, ignorance becomes established, wine is drunk, and adultery appears openly."
"4180","Ja'far ibn Mihran narrated to us, 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah al-Duba'i, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Madinah he stayed in the upper part of Madinah, in a quarter called Banu 'Amr ibn 'Awf, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed among them fourteen nights. Then he sent for the chiefs of Banu al-Najjar and they came with their swords slung. Anas said: It is as though I am looking at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on his mount, with Abu Bakr behind him, and the chiefs of Banu al-Najjar around him, until he alighted in the courtyard of Abu Ayyub. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray wherever prayer overtook him, and would pray in sheep pens. Then he ordered the building of the mosque, so he sent for the chiefs of Banu al-Najjar and they came. He said: O Banu al-Najjar, name a price for me for this wall of yours. They said: No, by Allah, we seek no price for it except to Allah. Anas said: In it was what I tell you: there were graves of the polytheists, there were ruins, and there were palm trees. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the graves of the polytheists exhumed, the ruins leveled, and the palms cut down. They placed the palms toward the qiblah of the mosque and made its doorposts of stone. He said: They began carrying that rock while chanting, with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among them, saying:"
"4181","Abu Yahya said: Ibn Abi al-Hudhayl narrated to me: 'Ammar ibn Yasir was a strong man, and would carry two stones. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he met him and pushed his chest, saying: Carry for me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began wiping dust from his head and chest, saying: Son of Sumayyah, the rebellious faction will kill you."
"4182","Abu Nasr 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz al-Qushayri al-Tammar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu 'Imran al-Jawni, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and there I was before a palace of gold. I said: Whose palace is this? They said: A young man of Quraysh. I thought it was mine, so I said: Who is he? They said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab. O Abu Hafs, were it not for what I know of your jealousy I would have entered it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, whom would I be jealous over - I would never be jealous toward you."
"4183","Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, 'Awbad ibn Abi 'Imran narrated to us, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Anas, perform ablution fully and your life will be increased; greet whomever you meet of my ummah and your good deeds will multiply; when you enter your house, greet whomever you meet of your household and the good of your house will multiply; and pray the Duha prayer, for it is the prayer of the penitent before you. And he said: O Anas, have mercy on the young, honor the old, and be among my companions."
"4184","Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, Ziyad ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, Abu 'Imran al-Jawni narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I do not recognize anything that was in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). It was said to him: Where is prayer, O Abu Hamzah? He said: Have you not done with prayer what you have come to know?"
"4185","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Musa informed us, from Abu 'Imran al-Jawni, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set a time for us in trimming the mustache, clipping the nails, and shaving the pubic hair - that they not be left more than forty days."
"4186","'Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh al-'Anbari narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu 'Imran al-Jawni, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah says to the lightest of the people of the Fire in punishment: Had you the world with all in it, would you ransom yourself with it? He says: Yes. He says: I wanted from you easier than this while you were in the loins of Adam: that you not associate, - I think he said: and I would not enter you into the Fire - but you refused except polytheism."
"4187","Abu Nasr al-Tammar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Zayd, and Yunus ibn 'Ubayd, and Humayd, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is he from whom people feel safe; the Muslim is he from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe; the emigrant is he who abandons evil; and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, no servant enters Paradise whose neighbor does not feel safe from his harms."
"4188","Mu'adh ibn Shu'bah narrated to us, Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, from Abu al-Haytham, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Anas: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When food is brought near to one of you while on his feet are sandals, let him remove his sandals, for it is more restful for the feet, and it is from the Sunnah."
"4189","'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Zayd, and Ja'far, and 'Abdullah ibn Rawahah, and gave the banner to Zayd. He said: What if all are struck? He said: Anas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) announced them to the people before the news came. He said: Zayd took the banner and was struck, then Ja'far took it and was struck, then 'Abdullah took it and was struck, then afterward a sword from among the swords of Allah - Khalid ibn al-Walid - took the banner. He said: He went on informing the people while his eyes shed tears."
"4190","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Zayd took the banner and was struck, then Ja'far took it and was struck, then 'Abdullah ibn Rawahah took it and was struck, then Khalid ibn al-Walid took it without command and Allah gave victory through him. It would not please them - or please me - that they were with us, while his eyes shed tears."
"4191","Isma'il ibn 'Abdullah ibn Khalid al-Qurashi narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah and Humayd ibn Hilal, from Anas, who said: I was riding behind Abu Talhah with my knee touching the knee of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they would call out with both together: with Hajj and 'Umrah."
"4192","Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I never saw anyone more merciful to dependents than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He had his son Ibrahim nursed at the farthest part of Madinah; her husband was a blacksmith, and he would come to him, and the boy would come to him with traces of smoke upon him, and he would embrace him and kiss him and smell him."
"4193","Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, who said: I saw Anas ibn Malik and al-Hasan praying on the day of 'Eid before the imam came out. He said: I saw Muhammad ibn Sirin come and sit without praying."
"4194","'Ubaydullah ibn Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh al-'Anbari narrated to us, my father narrated to us, 'Imran narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Abi Tamimah, who said: Anas grew weak for fasting, so he made a bowl of tharid and invited thirty poor persons and fed them."
"4195","Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Isma'il narrated to us, from Ayyub, from 'Amr ibn Sa'id, from Anas, who said: I never saw anyone more merciful to dependents than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ibrahim was being nursed in the outskirts of Madinah; he would set out with us with him and enter the house while it was filled with smoke - his foster father was a blacksmith - and he would take him and kiss him, then return. 'Amr said: When Ibrahim died, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ibrahim is my son; he died in infancy, and he has two foster mothers who will complete his nursing in Paradise."
"4196","Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from 'Amr ibn Sa'id, from Anas, who said: I never saw anyone more merciful to dependents than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and he mentioned the like."
"4197","Al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ayyub, from 'Amr ibn Sa'id, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the most merciful to children. He had a son being nursed in a quarter of Madinah; his foster father was a blacksmith, and he would come to him - with us with him - the house having been smoked as it was smoked, and he would smell him and kiss him, then return."
"4198","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Yahya ibn Yazid al-Huna'i, who said: I asked Anas ibn Malik about shortening prayer. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - when he went out a distance of three miles or three farsakhs - Shu'bah is the doubter - would pray two rak'ahs."
"4199","Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id al-Balkhi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Dinar al-Tahi narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Yazid, from Anas ibn Malik: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a man who divorced his wife three times, then she married a husband who died before consummating with her - may the first marry her? He said: No, until he tastes her little honey (i.e. consummates with her)."
"4200","Sa'id ibn Abi al-Rabi' narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Dinar narrated to us, with its chain."
